ivacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/59460737c9428262e242e0d09d5283ede5392a84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:07:36Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:07:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it''s containing window (#1930)\n\n* (feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it''s containing window\n\nWhile I want to leave the window as the default size, it''s convenient\nfor some workspaces (like the form workspace) to have a different display\nsize depending on the content they are displaying.\n\nWorkspace v1 accommodated this in a less sustainable way where a\nworkspace could modify it''s size while running. This change allows the\nsame overriding but only on a per-workspace basis. This does not\nintroduce a hook to programmatically control the size of the workspace.\n\nI also removed a CSS transition that only worked when shrinking the\nbrowser to tablet width. It seems we''re going with the workspace\n\"snapping\" without animation, so this is just for consistency.\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* (chore) Add docs","tree":{"sha":"c6b9695638f54ca02f797a033453459ae17c4155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/c6b9695638f54ca02f797a033453459ae17c4155"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/59460737c9428262e242e0d09d5283ede5392a84","verification":{"payload":"tree c6b9695638f54ca02f797a033453459ae17c4155\nparent 64eec9de063da2b2210092c275975760b6e15714\nauthor Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com> 1791209256 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791209256 +0000\n\n(feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it''s containing window (#1930)\n\n* (feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it''s containing window\n\nWhile I want to leave the window as the default size, it''s convenient\nfor some workspaces (like the form workspace) to have a different display\nsize depending on the content they are displaying.\n\nWorkspace v1 accommodated this in a less sustainable way where a\nworkspace could modify it''s size while running. This change allows the\nsame overriding but only on a per-workspace basis. This does not\nintroduce a hook to programmatically control the size of the workspace.\n\nI also removed a CSS transition that only worked when shrinking the\nbrowser to tablet width. It seems we''re going with the workspace\n\"snapping\" without animation, so this is just for consistency.\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* (chore) Add docs","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw68oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqVIQAKNiIw/nnTDEjqAgyhPxh7H6\nJT6x2/bN3U7All38ZZGcnRHXXMnQwdbKd7dfAqoN5Ab82ZPJ0cFb/lrJEs/Chj/F\nyPZf0ZudDU0UZsY37HMfswGbs/cge8rKbJmoF2puupmEI8VRmb2z1+j+kfQRHMe9\nyLMj21jjFsLNrz31vhFrU23AIg1qMzxPM+Yd5Sb8Je7y6rauzimSjgop/9Te1fFe\nOj4b/GTrT9Uf8tKQxP+rPQl32Mr2V8clAqbJJ6K61qU14ZKQl5bWNOToRe9w5tw8\n6efJi4Z0jQBbp/qRf/nWt9iiryDA8PDHf2C5u0ytLXQYjNRlcs61gu2dfOMwPl3s\nB63VdjwjkAwGgRcXYPLWmeRTI3vLTNouPO2bSki2OQh3Q8io0K3py1IXg0PioOXw\n9L