/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/3ae5ba8ce04628f740862fcc550e31a54d716167/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:08:51Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:08:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms (#1927)\n\n* (feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms\n\nAdds four pictograms for page headers that show a bare title today:\n\n- CohortsPictogram (omrs-pict-cohorts) for Cohort Builder: a two-by-three\n  grid of patients with two picked out in the darker teal.\n- ConceptDictionaryPictogram (omrs-pict-concept-dictionary) for the OCL\n  subscription page: an open book with an arrow coming down into it.\n- DataEntryPictogram (omrs-pict-data-entry) for Fast Data Entry: a paper\n  form with field lines above a keyboard.\n- ReportsPictogram (omrs-pict-reports) for Reports: four bars of uneven\n  height on a baseline, with the tallest one dark.\n\nEach is drawn to stay distinct from the existing set at 92px. Cohorts\nuses smaller figures in a grid rather than the few large figures in\npatients and service queues, concept dictionary is a book rather than\nthe box in metadata export, data entry adds a keyboard so it isn''t\nanother document, and reports is the set''s only chart. The drawings\nare new. Only ideas came from Carbon''s population--diagram, literature,\nkeyboard and chart--bar pictograms, and no Carbon path data was copied.\n\nRegisters the SVGs, adds the ids and component exports, and adds the\ncomponents to the styleguide mocks.\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>","tree":{"sha":"10d0ffa1a57c493723da7ad2f164bb322aa0fb6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/10d0ffa1a57c493723da7ad2f164bb322aa0fb6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/3ae5ba8ce04628f740862fcc550e31a54d716167","verification":{"payload":"tree 10d0ffa1a57c493723da7ad2f164bb322aa0fb6a\nparent 4cc27d388fb4a4fe49316791a20127dbb04e31ae\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1790950131 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790950131 +0300\n\n(feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms (#1927)\n\n* (feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms\n\nAdds four pictograms for page headers that show a bare title today:\n\n- CohortsPictogram (omrs-pict-cohorts) for Cohort Builder: a two-by-three\n  grid of patients with two picked out in the darker teal.\n- ConceptDictionaryPictogram (omrs-pict-concept-dictionary) for the OCL\n  subscription page: an open book with an arrow coming down into it.\n- DataEntryPictogram (omrs-pict-data-entry) for Fast Data Entry: a paper\n  form with field lines above a keyboard.\n- ReportsPictogram (omrs-pict-reports) for Reports: four bars of uneven\n  height on a baseline, with the tallest one dark.\n\nEach is drawn to stay distinct from the existing set at 92px. Cohorts\nuses smaller figures in a grid rather than the few large figures in\npatients and service queues, concept dictionary is a book rather than\nthe box in metadata export, data entry adds a keyboard so it isn''t\nanother document, and reports is the set''s only chart. The drawings\nare new. Only ideas came from Carbon''s population--diagram, literature,\nkeyboard and chart--bar pictograms, and no Carbon path data was copied.\n\nRegisters the SVGs, adds the ids and component exports, and adds the\ncomponents to the styleguide mocks.\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.o