/196801028d4926e16e050cb1623ada06db1e8ddf","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDE5NjgwMTAyOGQ0OTI2ZTE2ZTA1MGNiMTYyM2FkYTA2ZGIxZThkZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","sha":"40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd"}],"sha":"196801028d4926e16e050cb1623ada06db1e8ddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/196801028d4926e16e050cb1623ada06db1e8ddf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:11:09Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:11:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Let openmrs develop pick a port on hosts without IPv6 (#1903)\n\nisPortAvailable binds the port on both localhost and ::1, and treated any\nerror from the ::1 bind as the port being taken. On a host with IPv6\ndisabled, that bind fails with EAFNOSUPPORT for every port, so\n`openmrs develop --port <n>` always reported the port as in use and\n`openmrs develop` without --port scanned every port up to 65535 and gave\nup.\n\nWe now only treat the ::1 bind as a conflict when the error means\nsomething is actually listening there. EAFNOSUPPORT (IPv6 disabled) and\nEADDRNOTAVAIL (IPv6 enabled but no ::1 on the loopback) fall back to the\nIPv4 result.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119NcFRAE7ZNsubL4edUik3\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"90552118dce02c706434682682351bb2ad10c5eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/90552118dce02c706434682682351bb2ad10c5eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 90552118dce02c706434682682351bb2ad10c5eb\nparent c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1790673069 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790673069 +0300\n\n(fix) Let openmrs develop pick a port on hosts without IPv6 (#1903)\n\nisPortAvailable binds the port on both localhost and ::1, and treated any\nerror from the ::1 bind as the port being taken. On a host with IPv6\ndisabled, that bind fails with EAFNOSUPPORT for every port, so\n`openmrs develop --port <n>` always reported the port as in use and\n`openmrs develop` without --port scanned every port up to 65535 and gave\nup.\n\nWe now only treat the ::1 bind as a conflict when the error means\nsomething is actually listening there. EAFNOSUPPORT (IPv6 disabled) and\nEADDRNOTAVAIL (IPv6 enabled but no ::1 on the loopback) fall back to the\nIPv4 result.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119NcFRAE7ZNsubL4edUik3\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu4CtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQSMQAKfic3wROPmI/JBtiH4qOiph\ntElw+1CDKylvAsohufEJJ/VqktSuKe/OWGtRjoGaAH8rgZaG+Y29+bb889X56Dy/\nWUG8ETeqWFQFfYvC2CSA3nbHkzVb13v1uqHguj96HADTBx3wdzd0Cni88V1oNd5m\n+lfoRKYFYHnDC9pUilpk59mI/bvMICetjOT1/x3m/QgF8C73GtAHDRw9b4A2Vf6c\nrYao78PdTwAMUdcOGMDVMFS8mMn7okoLke5B+nzbMZhBDxZMY4Vb6H18t4w+flnp\n3Vs9doARohOd1gXj60z0msieBKIeDVAa/hYTD4aOJ6EFoYIWWVQNayIRQHMERlfD\n0eMUlt29jucCH9aooEPtUpPSDa1AUU1/2L6R7p77rbxtmUfDPupGgCOhi7ky/i6e\n6BxxuIOXSeHUEMQh05M8IycjWoBC+MaFW5Qw18qVGBhv97aQ8LKf2n57DTX6Jm4x\nNesoQTNsce3j/wLBMrtRoa2UR/AkQXlSvBYAfKVVRJtQ8SE/TBu9KswHJkINjDBf\nPfqUQ6327ttLLATCGkQtlI7xBMFGu/jj3VCuNfWfBXU5YizwXo7PkGm6bLx2Zxw0\nmN2A4O8Sn3pUoynY2AMNkDII0kMS4Q5W3OrJZjhPRA4BwqOaPDEf1A/AZIkwhl8N\nhp8eV1IA6rEH1GaAiJlC\n=vrqF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T09:11:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDQwZjlkMTgzNTZlY2YwM2RhYmQ0Mzk5NmY1ZjIwNWVmN2U1OWMyYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","sha":"c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0"}],"sha":"40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:17:38Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:17:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Place the app shell''s loading spinner and error page in the body grid''s app area (#1904)\n\n* (fix) Place the app shell''s loading spinner in the body grid''s app area\n\nThe app shell appends its startup spinner to <body>, which is a grid with\nnamed areas for the top nav, left nav, app roots and workspace. The\nspinner had no grid area, so the browser auto-placed it in a new row\nbelow those, in the first column. That column is sized min-content, so it\ngrew to the spinner''s width (about 84px) and pushed #omrs-apps-container\nto the right until the spinner was removed. The new row also starts below\nthe fold, so the spinner was never visible.\n\nPlacing the spinner in the appRoots area leaves the column widths alone\nand centers the spinner in the viewport. The spinner is removed right\nafter single-spa starts, before any page mounts into\n#omrs-apps-container, so the two don''t overlap.\n\nOn a cold load of /spa/system-administration this removes the two layout\nshifts the spinner caused, one when it''s added and one when it''s removed.\nCLS goes from 0.113 to 0.003 on localhost, and from 0.291 to 0.164 with\n4x CPU throttling on a 1.6 Mbps, 150 ms RTT connection.\n\n* Add a changeset for the loading spinner grid fix\n\nRecords a patch entry for @openmrs/esm-styleguide describing the spinner\nplacement fix, matching the changeset that other merged PRs in this repo\ninclude.\n\n* Place the fatal error page in the body grid''s app area too\n\nThe shell''s fatal error page had the same problem as the loading spinner.\nrenderFatalErrorPage() appends it to <body> without a grid area, so the\nbrowser auto-placed it in an extra row below the fold, inside the\nmin-content left nav column, which it then widened to fit its content. On\na real startup failure (the Intl.DurationFormat polyfill chunk failing to\nload), users saw a blank page with only an error toast.\n\nThis adds the error page to the spinner''s appRoots rule. min-width: 0\nstops a long error message in the code snippet from stretching the column\npast the viewport, the same way #omrs-apps-container does. The message\nincludes the failed chunk''s URL, so its width depends on the hostname:\nwith a realistic hostname, a 768px-wide tablet viewport overflowed by\n160px without it. The error page now fills the app area at tablet and\ndesktop widths and in RTL, with the heading and Reload button in view.\n\nAlso updates the changeset to cover the error page.\n\n* Document the body grid layout\n\nAdds a comment above the body grid that describes its areas and explains\nwhy anything rendered into <body> in the normal flow needs one. Without an\narea, the browser places it in a new row below the fold, in the left nav\ncolumn, which widens to fit it. Fixed-position containers aren''t affected.","tree":{"sha":"ee25b00d1d7d9320229aab9422229f042624f0f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/ee25b00d1d7d9320229aab9422229f042624f0f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","verification":{"payload":"tree ee25b00d1d7d9320229aab9422229f042624f0f1\nparent 7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1790630258 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790630258 +0300\n\n(fix) Place the app shell''s loading spinner and error page in the body grid''s app area (#1904)\n\n* (fix) Place the app shell''s loading spinner in the body grid''s app area\n\nThe app shell appends its startup spinner to <body>, which is a grid with\nnamed areas for the top nav, left nav, app roots and workspace. The\nspinner had no grid area, so the browser auto-placed it in a new row\nbelow those, in the first column. That column is sized min-content, so it\ngrew to the spinner''s width (about 84px) and pushed #omrs-apps-container\nto the right until the spinner was removed. The new row also starts below\nthe fold, so the spinner was never visible.\n\nPlacing the spinner in the appRoots area leaves the column widths alone\nand centers the spinner in the viewport. The spinner is removed right\nafter single-spa starts, before any page mounts into\n#omrs-apps-container, so the two don''t overlap.\n\nOn a cold load of /spa/system-administration this removes the two layout\nshifts the spinner caused, one when it''s added and one when it''s removed.\nCLS goes from 0.113 to 0.003 on localhost, and from 0.291 to 0.164 with\n4x CPU throttling on a 1.6 Mbps, 150 ms RTT connection.\n\n* Add a changeset for the loading spinner grid fix\n\nRecords a patch entry for @openmrs/esm-styleguide describing the spinner\nplacement fix, matching the changeset that other merged PRs in this repo\ninclude.\n\n* Place the fatal error page in the body grid''s app area too\n\nThe shell''s fatal error page had the same problem as the loading spinner.\nrenderFatalErrorPage() appends it to <body> without a grid area, so the\nbrowser auto-placed it in an extra row below the fold, inside the\nmin-content left nav column, which it then widened to fit its content. On\na real startup failure (the Intl.DurationFormat polyfill chunk failing to\nload), users saw a blank page with only an error toast.\n\nThis adds the error page to the spinner''s appRoots rule. min-width: 0\nstops a long error message in the code snippet from stretching the column\npast the viewport, the same way #omrs-apps-container does. The message\nincludes the failed chunk''s URL, so its width depends on the hostname:\nwith a realistic hostname, a 768px-wide tablet viewport overflowed by\n160px without it. The error page now fills the app area at tablet and\ndesktop widths and in RTL, with the heading and Reload button in view.\n\nAlso updates the changeset to cover the error page.\n\n* Document the body grid layout\n\nAdds a comment above the body grid that describes its areas and explains\nwhy anything rendered into <body> in the normal flow needs one. Without an\narea, the browser places it in a new row below the fold, in the left nav\ncolumn, which widens to fit it. Fixed-position containers aren''t affected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqutlyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANvYQAJY91g0JnAaBXgIYPgg6LV53\nA1rjntEiNspJwj5KjVCKYMHsxpUzE6rJMYRlPk7vnN9+EnBuvofobhxyrgRube5T\nMr3WyYGOrTila8ajqjjLPvvZjGi3Dr5kEWaR55RtPyNF3mfjvKUWe6RBonaFIK0v\nP1If8U8Cs98ZmSoH9Wz3b2a455ArDxzRH28C6XhV5uS0vRgcpVwwRcC316oPSmDU\n/OSQOFDbzHGSwoooRi1hwWh7fztw2RJHKhnmS+d3r14SNSqhFTwZKGGlmMZ37aHr\nfUsDLjVD6R55nMzQTYXplD5PXhXIDXH3MrO6P3dBuhqQGWVLrRnMtv8FBk4Kns0N\ntkaTsdetfNaBXEN/QkN/irIyyoIHV4+sJMqustGpcdYOvFeqWApRr7QRCPMjfmfH\nvDdhDL2VyE2v1YOoQrSer/8OWs6vmQPTFnkLA1zgO9NdmEXYSRwtagtj3bMHohb4\ndKkJLfU5vhsBEDOa2NXFm0Mw1z+Qv3Jj5qDKfgKJ4TA11ilHplUqGgn5VU8/92Xz\njJ9ywAxvBnB4Y7TT1n+bBpOjCBR9YWXxVjNGkDBLjQOeH78spzUr6oY46lTsyPfU\nFfPHSx6oMfbh/wcy3DCXk8CqdwGw3LlTs8GofPacav7tQv4lHY8ocCrAF9pMG2vQ\nfS5PvmiPSSCcfzV8rpax\n=Rpc7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T21:17:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKGM2YjdjNzZmMWI4MTExNzIwMzY5MjUyZjNjYzIwY2Y5YTlkMWU2YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","sha":"7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527"}],"sha":"c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:25:32Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:25:32Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"message":"(fix) Stop the E2E dependency caches from overwriting each other\n\nScope each node_modules cache in the E2E workflow to its own repo. The\nesm-core caches now exclude e2e_repo/**, and the cache for the checked-out\nrepo only covers e2e_repo/**/node_modules and includes the repo name in its\nkey.\n\nBoth caches used to cache **/node_modules from the workspace root, so each\none matched esm-core''s node_modules as well as e2e_repo''s. Restoring the\nother repo''s cache overwrote esm-core''s fresh install with the esm-core\nnode_modules saved alongside it, and the esm-core cache step then saved\nthat mixed tree under esm-core''s lockfile key.\n\nAfter the turbo upgrade, the patient-chart cache still held esm-core''s\npre-upgrade node_modules. It was restored over the new install and saved\nas main''s esm-core cache. Runs that restored that entry skipped yarn\ninstall, and yarn turbo failed with \"Couldn''t find a script named turbo\"\nbecause node_modules/.yarn-state.yml still described turbo 2.5.2.\n\ndeploy-pages uses the same path list as the E2E esm-core cache so the two\nkeep sharing entries. Changing the paths also changes the cache version,\nso entries saved with the old paths are no longer restored.","tree":{"sha":"0eaff37622afcb0a19e5e26024888793cfe090d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/0eaff37622afcb0a19e5e26024888793cfe090d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDdjZjZmZWY2OTg2YmM2OGE2ZmE1NWMyZjU2ZWM5NmYzOTkyNzE1Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20","sha":"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20"}],"sha":"7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/7cf6fef6986bc68a6fa55c2f56ec96f399271527"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:08:46Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:08:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\n\n* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\n\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\nfuture version.\n\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\n\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`''s opts\n\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\n\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\n\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\n\n* More clean-up\n\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\n\n* Fixup changesets","tree":{"sha":"90e9a6790f7b311a174b8472ac98d0262411132a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/90e9a6790f7b311a174b8472ac98d0262411132a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20","verification":{"payload":"tree 90e9a6790f7b311a174b8472ac98d0262411132a\nparent d45e87b01ba5db3d8431223135db4bd8e7425a67\nauthor Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com> 1790618926 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790618926 +0300\n\n(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\n\n* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\n\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\nfuture version.\n\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\n\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`''s opts\n\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\n\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\n\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\n\n* More clean-up\n\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\n\n* Fixup changesets","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquq0uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUIUQAKGqeW5T/dbHeivKqoJjeLnM\nXkDT4mRJgmp4TAKCO9iCeOAktAWtommNBNr33WHz9E4WdyndWgrJjYiMtTPAfGvm\nk8asoVFSxB0QLstuM9jFKRANOQRp1y/jbvDrxdJKYH1BeFS4fgk9q8j0/aA9RErS\nU3kkQyGgLHkY7K3vRVPYivKdN1Zg+UZwRyzyG1pDMIoSG2tE1dby5ASZB4RRlm0p\nvW/N/0lU8xQMyQREYdYviJODhEsNfJYZQ2nhiv7WQpNXo9rgNu3fU4JVMbGNUILK\nosndjAtAoY2PmJrOXuolDPGSVTsppy2nXF6WY5/nkJJjvHkRcaFUUEb+mk5Ypp2e\nP5pXuMjC4WPBUBFeATzoaV71FZUhRR81fQVH/18HnSUNolJt9ryp3FFf7e3NfLAH\neB1pRNed4JK24mhLNoczAAdHcjiPAECM0KhohZiuyNbEU0VCB5P/cr5yG5cyRgn7\n6Q0TidDlgLMasFGAV64hDxK9mr+mcRvBNaOhmQf629Aa6XnOE+qITxQ7Eo3YkKoz\nsPu8k6ReHKelEtfzELoq9j7NM57HXVoWeWlZI3XQtjxC++ROOM5JM+eV3xjW6EqS\n+eovssallrQ7g0Bc/uYwBcZEweo/01R5KyJMsw/1Gr4bz/O3+yMoO4LXzulFfweF\naCMhVdmPHN0ZmVFHjuZB\n=fgaU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T18:08:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_eve