828b7dc2e26a80ebebece8734d684bd06c"}],"sha":"43e9a2e0f2e61c51c7cd40ee254da1e1c4396cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/43e9a2e0f2e61c51c7cd40ee254da1e1c4396cc6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/bddd76828b7dc2e26a80ebebece8734d684bd06c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:35:16Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T16:35:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Pass the browserslist targets to the app shell''s CSS minimizer (#1885)\n\n* (fix) Pass the browserslist targets to the app shell''s CSS minimizer\n\nThe app shell''s rspack config never set optimization.minimizer, so production builds used rspack''s default Lightning CSS minimizer with its own browser targets. Those targets are old enough that Lightning CSS downlevels every logical property in the shell''s CSS, including all of Carbon, into physical properties guarded by :lang() language lists, repeated for :-webkit-any and :-moz-any, plus mirrored rules for RTL languages. On main that is 6,594 fallback rules and about two thirds of 3 MB of CSS.\n\nThe shared rspack and webpack configs for modules already pass browserslist-config-openmrs to their CSS minimizers. This does the same for the shell, reusing the browserTargets the config already passes to swc. Setting minimizer replaces rspack''s default pair, so the JS minimizer is listed alongside it.\n\nThe styleguide stylesheet is excluded from the minimizer. The config compiles it with sass, names it after a hash of that output and copies it in as a static file, so minifying it afterwards changed its bytes under a name that no longer matched them. Sass already emits it compressed; leaving it alone costs about 3 KB gzipped and keeps the name honest.\n\nBuilt from the same commit before and after: shell CSS goes from 3.03 MB to 1.11 MB raw in total and the main stylesheet from 163 KB to 104 KB gzipped, with no fallback rules left. JS output is byte-identical; only the entry file''s hash changes because it embeds the renamed CSS chunk names.\n\n* Mark the copied styleguide stylesheet as minified instead of excluding it by name\n\nThe exclude regex encoded the 16-character hash length used to name the\nfile, so the two had to move together and nothing checked that they did.\nSetting info.minimized on the copy pattern tells the CSS minimizer the\nasset is already minified, whatever it is called. Output is unchanged.\n\n* chore: Remove redundant styleguide copy comment\n\nRemove the explanatory comment above the styleguide copy pattern following review feedback. Keep the minimized asset metadata unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"f7d373a7b323f98f48e798be1f71f02c81cfb3b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/f7d373a7b323f98f48e798be1f71f02c81cfb3b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/bddd76828b7dc2e26a80ebebece8734d684bd06c","verification":{"payload":"tree f7d373a7b323f98f48e798be1f71f02c81cfb3b3\nparent 8173bbe9f9938ff3202e6a8a0ea3dba4c622757c\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1790094916 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790094916 +0300\n\n(fix) Pass the browserslist targets to the app shell''s CSS minimizer (#1885)\n\n* (fix) Pass the browserslist targets to the app shell''s CSS minimizer\n\nThe app shell''s rspack config never set optimization.minimizer, so production builds used rspack''s default Lightning CSS minimizer with its own browser targets. Those targets are old enough that Lightning CSS downlevels every logical property in the shell''s CSS, including all of Carbon, into physical properties guarded by :lang() language lists, repeated for :-webkit-any and :-moz-any, plus mirrored rules for RTL languages. On main that is 6,594 fallback rules and about two thirds of 3 MB of CSS.\n\nThe shared rspack and webpack configs for modules already pass browserslist-config-openmrs to their CSS minimizers. This does the same for the shell, reusing the browserTargets the config already passes to swc. Setting minimizer replaces rspack''s default pair, so the JS minimizer is listed alongside it.\n\nThe styleguide stylesheet is excluded from the minimizer. The config compiles it with sass, names it after a hash of that output and copies it in as a static file, so minifying it afterwards changed its bytes under a name that no longer matched them. Sass already emits it compressed; leaving it alone costs about 3 KB gzipped and keeps the name honest.\n\nBuilt from the same commit before and after: shell CSS goes from 3.03 MB to 1.11 MB raw in total and the main stylesheet from 163 KB to 104 KB gzipped, with no fallback rules left. JS output is byte-identical; only the entry file''s hash changes because it embeds the renamed CSS chunk names.\n\n* Mark the copied styleguide stylesheet as minified instead of excluding it by name\n\nThe exclude regex encoded the 16-character hash length used to name the\nfile, so the two had to move together and nothing checked that they did.\nSetting info.minimized on the copy pattern tells the CSS minimizer the\nasset is already minified, whatever it is called. Output is unchanged.\n\n* chore: Remove redundant styleguide copy comment\n\nRemove the explanatory comment above the styleguide copy pattern following review feedback. Keep the minimized asset metadata unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsq5ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA34cQADccFYC/UFa53TToVIIAYLSN\ndhuUOyXGk0OetOBqXILO5zUOpnB8Emd4UwPw3HeLDxWOVi3W0BCZ6RwuZY8NJxBY\nL+nom1Fn2U+qVZegysqoFi8nsI8OW9P1OqEFAti96UEtrTqtsLCO1zTqg5dKI8XH\nsGfxQw0wKhl39xHObwIU4mcw345sitfNZsGwyMH4SwwAJ8EdSc9XSTgj/vhd1atV\nxk/UGKXnam03XXy9Ben3OZzkwnMw6M1c48kcr5InHK0Vt8htaVq7I1B0rKhvA1Xk\nq0rb62AQci4ygx6OghU0IqY8AGG+DgbtbtnzrpBo/qJFFgma4XTtoljEU/WbuUp5\nRZzTdjXapQb4azZ5Y0lobhvvP0emhJS3rZvzPEUhYjExGxwJfsUc1HUWuYuKdCmA\nKMFrmnozTpraod+B+YPcPHrhOpXZ9e94uVTc24WMex2R03vBh4cTVc+CZjjn2iWm\nE+E1kzAnRgKh+GcLwYZ+WTRIXqraAGep1nrFq7WcD1cIR7JE/0vccL5ZbjcRJENH\nWfS4PH/qDHTSs6LVcVbvbkDWknTthX+siJiUKLtSnl8To03PekqrQ2Rq6meiyWHY\npxb1paeCYziL9uUU424WkmOBPDywYy/GKuKw2Y7Fa9deOIbIi0z8mBQjjvt/qP0R\ny5K12rkRCGkHKLnBEO+0\n=5z5t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T16:35:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"ht