"8173bbe9f9938ff3202e6a8a0ea3dba4c622757c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/8173bbe9f9938ff3202e6a8a0ea3dba4c622757c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:22:04Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:22:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)\n\n* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\n\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\nnote''s own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\n\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it''s set. We leave\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\nto invalidate it.\n\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\nAPI docs.\n\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\n\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\nencounter to load.\n\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\n\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\nthey have already loaded.","tree":{"sha":"3a226f4e15709c1ec0c63f5efd2e1f3df2e1bcd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/3a226f4e15709c1ec0c63f5efd2e1f3df2e1bcd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a226f4e15709c1ec0c63f5efd2e1f3df2e1bcd9\nparent 92bf2449a4eef5836fbb8abd20fbb6d752633ea6\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1789752124 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789752124 +0000\n\n(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)\n\n* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\n\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\nnote''s own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\n\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it''s set. We leave\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\nto invalidate it.\n\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\nAPI docs.\n\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\n\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\nencounter to load.\n\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\n\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\nthey have already loaded.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrXM8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAntsQADtX0yT6/DrvXMAjBQZLF/1E\nZhQ8pfIfp4SGuZZ5BTNwrKuhuE7Pj5Ns9TPnpM6eu1tyLiiOrWFA08+LphNfZYqt\nPomG23wwqzP65jc1Z5cwESIxnlVBi4uxayxvt0I8zogxaiE2UXDGtZeTdbvJ60FA\n61q0YMVb0nts9CEVOuep2Druww/aN1gh7AoWykQPK6seSNg3axFtXXWENJTqnvWP\nPm4BISGnJ7IHqgFEf3iPKA1ON++yy8xxszz4JHr8fHEo5FhXo6vi6CU7qT4uw6W/\nElrQJlOI5YN35hxxnaLEzPT9Tp3fa1IR1LEVaGoCZmntkm1xacTSbc622DGC9N2V\n0gEQvIbe4JXRog65IjV4cD6zBAZDi7DEHoWAFrYNaescqlGxafYVyhcniTN8aurQ\nINnLYvDFk08ibDk4Q2Eacv2gQioaOOdMGQhDZ5sHRQP5JE7wX9jSMcpxnuVAa4WO\n6WvIc2CGM7+C0CUDpda2Td1AqBgzWRRHnadw7YRa2auvQqnTcSt+Fb/oXam3Pscd\nj3ajgMSlYAIcEhMYrMKCCj+GOizii4yZqIqxeihs1/pEP1blF8E6HEv8n1N05wO