he `SKIP_IF_BROKEN` state. This can include any DOM nodes it was\npreviously attached to. We cannot fully clean-up after single-spa, but\nsince we control the prop object we pass to it, we can clean-up the\n`domElement` single-spa stores there, which reduces most of the memory\npressure this causes.\n\nThe cost here is that every parcel receives a copy of the props passed\nto it so we''re not modifying (and clearing!) the callers props.","tree":{"sha":"a600c0dfa2261e1806387c1835d1fb55b664d384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/a600c0dfa2261e1806387c1835d1fb55b664d384"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/003926fef9be3dffb14a13c84ea65be62cc162fe","verification":{"payload":"tree a600c0dfa2261e1806387c1835d1fb55b664d384\nparent 227abd2a9a475a851015feb2f9a5b910f283e215\nauthor Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com> 1789375897 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789375897 +0300\n\n(fix) Release broken parcel DOM references (#1874)\n\n* (fix) Release broken parcel DOM references\n\nWhen a parcel rejects during unmount, single-spa retains the parcel entry\nin the `SKIP_IF_BROKEN` state. This can include any DOM nodes it was\npreviously attached to. We cannot fully clean-up after single-spa, but\nsince we control the prop object we pass to it, we can clean-up the\n`domElement` single-spa stores there, which reduces most of the memory\npressure this causes.\n\nThe cost here is that every parcel receives a copy of the props passed\nto it so we''re not modifying (and clearing!) the callers props.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp7WZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4jsQAHd1oUsIISKq0fFYJ4GkyNqg\nSSU+vZV+sMn0N0x2gGemBcNtHw6sQ8E/KIwBqacKX0N9N7Xk7sFJ5LTxqqZ+EEgi\nApWaFvfLyQNE87QcJvWHoUqwkwk6KLQ6CFavIq3IeadvpBte+eYtqd6KflYjHKPr\nGjkXGyPmRg3daRH8xtOICfL+LDtcN5HWDSN4SK9HyGxTm254KSUpVOzBO8KErYPh\nIXp6EjnOuqwqN4LaTNP8n/Hl5KZRF2CA6u1ko8RKuJcoSiBYtvwi0EPot8Ypxx1Z\nUI