e215","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDIyN2FiZDJhOWE0NzVhODUxMDE1ZmViMmY5YTViOTEwZjI4M2UyMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","sha":"6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806"}],"sha":"227abd2a9a475a851015feb2f9a5b910f283e215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/227abd2a9a475a851015feb2f9a5b910f283e215"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:55:33Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:55:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)\n\n* (fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa\n\nsingle-spa''s \"timeouts\" actually become `setTimeout()` calls that are\nnot cleared, even when the event they are waiting for has already\nhappened. The upshot of this is that pushing the 15s hard timeout for\nlifecycles to single-spa wound up holding references to unmounted apps\nunconditionally for 15s, even after the actual contents had unmounted.\n\nBy moving the hard timeouts into our framework and reverting to\nsingle-spa''s defaults, we greatly reduce the window that single-spa will\nhold the references to its default of 3s. Short of patching single-spa,\nthis seems like the best way we can work around this issue.\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Address review feedback\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>","tree":{"sha":"5fbc94ca5124ad099cbc163886dbd64f153a0fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/5fbc94ca5124ad099cbc163886dbd64f153a0fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","verification":{"payload":"tree 5fbc94ca5124ad099cbc163886dbd64f153a0fa6\nparent 818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb\nauthor Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com> 1789156533 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789156533 -0400\n\n(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)\n\n* (fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa\n\nsingle-spa''s \"timeouts\" actually become `setTimeout()` calls that are\nnot cleared, even when the event they are waiting for has already\nhappened. The upshot of this is that pushing the 15s hard timeout for\nlifecycles to single-spa wound up holding references to unmounted apps\nunconditionally for 15s, even after the actual contents had unmounted.\n\nBy moving the hard timeouts into our framework and reverting to\nsingle-spa''s defaults, we greatly reduce the window that single-spa will\nhold the references to its default of 3s. Short of patching single-spa,\nthis seems like the best way we can work around this issue.\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Address review feedback\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpFy1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXI0QAFLAFe7bf9CUVj/kk9q00bSe\n78PkrU2ahzH3Xn1FMJuKTxIU+MEsKwQBQPFcr6/RWaIXIxOoIHlZKHUDWDZ4+8Zz\nBtxOEqY2vbKdKPH4o8UnQ2IQKstGikMDorm7RLH8Xdza8iwgPkXMXwU8d7G8J1oK\nC9axCciWhWf7wf6433738u6KQDQD2MmjXmPotOT+UTHoV64dFVmMCeMt7xkGOVQS\ndbRBN5/0/aRZggcHDrHIuTXjV+Dg1b7ht/AHwBHiHhPVd5CqQwxyHFHLszqOKLGw\nIWkdYDcwFzvd0ZkRDAIlKMMCZwxipfmXcojPk6R8ojqJe9n4ebshRhk4MtTwaVMQ\nFP/SJrB3PyJ4auF/040776/hJAPbl9nc+Qr1O1kORUhQdWILCtq6YU+dIHVdFsRp\ncZSt95mx+RatlJSTkOMuTSpSNSgiRQvYgVK46twFEIgV/4xntXzUeCuIf909DX9a\nsPn1hH5t51fDSlJRRXandAP6uXcYUZJvnLeBFbAMBKcIdVvxcgasn9WtxOCRE9tc\n2u1ouavuY7Z0giK6SHuOhzoLXN3FJxwDyTVezHausTVk900v2mxtyA1sND8Kcrqm\nJXUTbpaFmHC5kZnThvjuNvlmA9XY+6ATYtgaGhNyhN0oTrlyL+aW8SmvheUiaNsQ\nEPv81ydPkb8ldK/O/q/A\n=jNjp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T19:55:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDZlYzE4OTMwYzJlNmU2ZDdiN2JhOTA2MmMwMTUxMTQ1NDdiZTk4MDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb","sha":"818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb"}],"sha":"6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T18:20:35Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T18:20:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\n\n* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\n\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\nbasically ensuring we''re using a consistent browserlist.\n\nThis also removes the \"main\" chunk we were generating, but which was\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\nloader and then the index chunk.\n\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\n\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\n\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\n\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\n\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Fix failing test on CI","tree":{"sha":"888bd2cced65584c0852bcf7cabb2fa466c9df18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/888bd2cced65584c0852bcf7cabb2fa466c9df18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 888bd2cced65584c0852bcf7cabb2fa466c9df18\nparent 2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\nauthor Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com> 1789064435 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789064435 +0300\n\n(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\n\n* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\n\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\nbasically ensuring we''re using a consistent browserlist.\n\nThis also removes the \"main\" chunk we were generating, but which was\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\nloader and then the index chunk.\n\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\n\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\n\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\n\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\n\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Fix failing test on CI","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqovTzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACocQAFaHwRs0OelBiIET0aRO1vvU\nQ1kZYYCgIbVQvOinmIZeJG3gXVjrFszjEdyhsPdaRE03Rj1Qq449E1HTq0UQi8z3\n4Txs3bygCgrqkAG9nkNAr4tFBTfcMm2yUETWse5ymZ2gVzMZhuJSQZN8ZlO4q9+e\nFFdVoG1skDi538STf/aL0LNRvmYi0o0S6hzf5QeM1GCqU8oBeRif+DUO6riXzx0y\nVjja6Ufh2BZF+8Z96KwbZqkjyrO/NwKZHvfXm0y0krFOAG0hag/XKyTgEYeWVKrk\nPyL4avDSNtMaXWz/sb/ThsynkSz8d4Vx6of65A21b4xKribkbdD2Sf3WXbHjruqV\ny9OJOaddzDrZuNLAlk7Z7lz7XeZCo13xVF7FdRQEotB3ZIFkMPhGYWwdUGWWDeR6\nB70YXw4LtN7HBUMCFlgwlQVKI5Cp9fOtApGcHLvo7LT5TC/hrIOz5XPYsCISY6i+\n/AZmQhy5BlaKhMu+DRyKwpL1COjNhpVKYu8oO9PS9nhJpVKLqZcdseC10gfwsxB2\nV2kOUCDKzZKAYEe8voi8IJEwuz4Qv/zpu4Y7Gj4xvzCj5H11kZBMgjL7lAvqnOLU\nut4NOn4+1myBKm+5FpovmjwWv8b1Jp5GpKq90mEJJVA9cr5FGRHwiBXclDixcr6V\n9BBVPcyJB9nN8eG4ess8\n=Xh0i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T18:20:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_ur