b-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/6d24172954e6ed691318848239e157642f6e9db5","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDZkMjQxNzI5NTRlNmVkNjkxMzE4ODQ4MjM5ZTE1NzY0MmY2ZTlkYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de","sha":"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de"}],"sha":"6d24172954e6ed691318848239e157642f6e9db5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/6d24172954e6ed691318848239e157642f6e9db5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T18:46:10Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T18:46:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\n\nThis PR overhauls the extension system''s internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\n\nBreakages:\n\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store''s state, but the state directly.\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e87f50c260789914008f685a1886cfb36ccbe3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/1e87f50c260789914008f685a1886cfb36ccbe3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e87f50c260789914008f685a1886cfb36ccbe3f\nparent da70f7fd6691df7db8c5739f073b08f271278381\nauthor Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com> 1788374770 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788374770 -0400\n\n(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\n\nThis PR overhauls the extension system''s internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\n\nBreakages:\n\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store''s state, but the state directly.\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmG7yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP9QQAIls3+fWBO/M4EfoSBmXVlAl\njwct23B0njjfr1TFNVl03CAuzc1rlcKpJz0Dem5yM7ysGQ6FS9oF9PVeDLPhMfX5\n/3wQA4kUBbsd+19+Ap4boTFful/7rGHSyDK0MCE6KREFL2F0FRZWPs1CbdMLsCVk\n6PlRk41bIKgFzMz7Xz2w7dUAcMMSalZFhQSHocAo45TKDYsNbZrL85ejlhaqZLD1\nOX9+lLuW3WEFS3+25RAV8LvhOqBiSCsPW3F18HzDDPWHxNywgl7I6GAyj7uOk6Li\neaxJXIVyXBAp9DJKuFnEBb377IWTe8ky8S7/k90BRkeenZw9WSdOWpAUs27qFqy+\nTJTwkMVuwXAZS2gf2fEl3k9ysOpcNZLOBvdTdDaEb5HC4iHquTJVwN8QPtOVtL58\nbSW6YtGaSc/b4HH0L8IN3CkyQ1R6g5AbipgzWEU855hzw+EAd3q/kF+TxTuS5giK\nQS5HSfcBSivrogAhOD2MvE7FgdHBYCGaeoEzK4kLNG+x4fQR3GNWE3O3VhuE9cZ1\nV5rFf+wsgmIVTt1p4qsh6PBF30wcvROWWoFFCqX51JHGfCyUA4ZcJjWa390qUYcS\nxPSq2xL0JVxAm9TKs3NPiixGsriLDhpOi+tde1c3azm3fJTI1EecnvBnXcW0jQ91\n7q+530my6hnZkWpZma23\n=LtOz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T18:46:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}",