e_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDlmMGM2YWE4MzFmMzdmZmNhZjE2N2E3MDk2YjA3ZWMzZTk2YTA0MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7","sha":"5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7"}],"sha":"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T11:44:46Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T11:44:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0 (#1841)\n\n* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0\n\nThis bumps `@openmrs/eslint-config` to [2.1.0](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-eslint-config/releases/tag/v2.1.0) which allows `typeof import(...)` annotations in test and mock files. That lets up drop the `consistent-type-imports` disable comments from our tests. While at it, this also tightens up some mock typings: wrapper args are now typed using `Parameters<typeof...>`, the `useConfig` casts in the log tests are narrower, and a few unused imports are removed.\n\n* Restore behavior the lint fixes accidentally changed\n\nThe openmrsComponentDecorator mock in esm-react-utils lost its currying\nwhen the component param got typed. The real API takes options first,\nthen the component, and the mock ships in the published\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, so the two need to match. Keep the type\nannotation, restore the currying.\n\nThe Logo test fixtures are whole config objects, so cast them back to\nConfigSchema instead of double-casting through unknown to the nested\nlogo type.","tree":{"sha":"3d099188efda304870ff2a296e419edb26ea4e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/3d099188efda304870ff2a296e419edb26ea4e0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d099188efda304870ff2a296e419edb26ea4e0e\nparent 6459e985e0fd79ccb2ca3f78795455307d67cd98\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1787139886 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787139886 +0300\n\n(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0 (#1841)\n\n* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0\n\nThis bumps `@openmrs/eslint-config` to [2.1.0](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-eslint-config/releases/tag/v2.1.0) which allows `typeof import(...)` annotations in test and mock files. That lets up drop the `consistent-type-imports` disable comments from our tests. While at it, this also tightens up some mock typings: wrapper args are now typed using `Parameters<typeof...>`, the `useConfig` casts in the log tests are narrower, and a few unused imports are removed.\n\n* Restore behavior the lint fixes accidentally changed\n\nThe openmrsComponentDecorator mock in esm-react-utils lost its currying\nwhen the component param got typed. The real API takes options first,\nthen the component, and the mock ships in the published\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, so the two need to match. Keep the type\nannotation, restore the currying.\n\nThe Logo test fixtures are whole config objects, so cast them back to\nConfigSchema instead of double-casting through unknown to the nested\nlogo type.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhZcuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj0wQAApH0czfqbC+Wy0pNj9/Oi0D\npmNV5GjaJHgfFSc3R+Y1DTrra/nrPT2DLEb1eI6f/a8fNpFfr2VkST276CyJSr/I\nZpidvu2GaS/8O7GkC5D3CT0rRBaSbiLP5xEzkV/L6AROgfs0HT3RJkzojy2ZPsHf\n9I9v0LRaLV+wOIyXPGaDkGYSnStlBiBhGkuFtl00O9Ax21mqfWyw9xbohX16IN3T\n8B+ZaKT/S4tvxMghHmdORH96+IFT8atxouSO2mlzjG/f8n8ePERjCzPnFUPZn240\nZLKRVE5vCo0iaJhO0lPJYm4my9Gr5kfKBbZ9LSeLkQoUoFevaNisaCwUQiD0oGJ4\n+5fSsD9VHcxWaxZjA5p6Na6Ou2w5SQZw4IpHto/z6Je1txjaQBeuHThB+jete05B\n8wtgGFOsXpn2yJDWvl47A0hDHQmCZq66/8ib9/g0g133wqk9jsk3mxhBojsc9Asr\nvi3JoCppi304ipn6vGLew1YDKvihj/YKVsq6wdtwidPSAp/krKuWmGTwAw7Oyi6z\nUHUfex5iN1y0bH54B0shsiAHF/LSp8pbX99/47lodRK6Z+u9Odo5LaPghKNlV+C5\nLOAHzjVkeK0M42yJu2ryAUTXgzqXZ0f0O4smMeLjzUWydutZfyJLnLZOYZcldxic\nS5GnXZrBrUUYFWhPq1yg\n=HfUJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T11:44:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7","node_id":"C_kwDOEUJ_kNoAKDVkMTg0ZjAwN2NhODg2NjZlZmFmN2QyNzZjMGNhZmE5NDUwNzM2Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commit/6459e985e0fd79ccb2ca3f78795455307d67cd98","sha":"6459e985e0fd79ccb2ca3f78795455307d67cd98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/6459e985e0fd79ccb2ca3f78795455307d67cd98"}],"sha":"5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/6459e985e0fd79ccb2ca3f78795455307d67cd98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:35:36Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:35:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(chore) Pin e2e CI installs to the lockfile (#1847)\n\nInstall Playwright browsers with yarn instead of npx in the e2e\nworkflow, so the step runs the playwright binary from the\nlockfile-pinned @playwright/test package rather than whatever npx\nresolves.\n\nBuild the e2e Docker image with yarn install --immutable, so the image\nalways installs exactly the locked dependency tree. This requires\ncopying packages/apps into the Docker build context. Without them, yarn\nprunes the missing app workspaces from the lockfile, and an immutable\ninstall fails with YN0028.\n\nBoth installs were flagged by SonarCloud (S8543 and S6505) for using\nunpinned or unenforced dependency versions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f6ef1b60acfafbb9eb7a18909cc103f346eb163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/1f6ef1b60acfafbb9eb7a18909cc103f346eb163"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/6459e985e0fd79ccb2ca3f78795455307d67cd98","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f6ef1b60acfafbb9eb7a18909cc103f346eb163\nparent 4d587a86da1133560d3322eea2d6bbdc75362b58\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1787128536 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787128536 +0300\n\n(chore) Pin e2e CI installs to the lockfile (#1847)\n\nInstall Playwright browsers with yarn instead of npx in the e2e\nworkflow, so the step runs the playwright binary from the\nlockfile-pinned @playwright/test package rather than whatever npx\nresolves.\n\nBuild the e2e Docker image with yarn install --immutable, so the image\nalways installs exactly the locked dependency tree. This requires\ncopying packages/apps into the Docker build context. Without them, yarn\nprunes the missing app workspaces from the lockfile, and an immutable\ninstall fails with YN0028.\n\nBoth installs were flagged by SonarCloud (S8543 and S6505) for using\nunpinned or unenforced dependency versions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhWrYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmJEQAEMn/J1cc0cVOvzqaptnoUVN\nKmMlU2jqqvGy0Sft7YNr0Y/uI4oteWcVyU4CDhbRHavUfM0cyJu2hWvRhWLrMTHQ\njM0Nb94l45J1cE92B/Juf8jKS9fe+eBbEEtVC68SzUxa/LKdwwtT4LJltskLIMCK\nUQB8wGYyRdqh9dk74w13zxUqP7+G6fxmUtqlFRkJh4z9qzZBu59/W94EWNzVxqj7\njeC8q7PHXFJaqTiu7JgWjH56pU8pI7Xa2QE6I1hk8PXDJUCwQcW+WGV0VsX41C6D\nM5aQqWhI0jLw5Ga6/CQUD5BuqGGs643oCS21/ULSj/Lveu8lVBrn4k1gY6wAAaGW\nQm56dzLn1Bs2EbUwlqP5dh8EYFMoTLRvbTqyD+q2RZtOwwvOGDly6xOIB9JQ4ISp\nLzjUw6Wbd9K4lh2pT/4KqEOKvQdzoYQirttzWyG5QW1z24+Hr4aenEB3p982ivYS\nuUgz3sGKg1XxH9anRsPy1ivs6Hvmb2ry6L7D9iq7OhB2PjR0a+FQwdZHgXrWzkfO\nWEti0xbXXppGuhO3qoI2sOsiQxtzshjD+2yzMxYVd31IjJnp2jNELoE4hyZkBJuA\nHcHYA1GGDag7WLBzjMyyrTt1H4ceZXUL0kpWnSiqk9DGJyegGHDHDFUiBeV13iv+\nI3iLDQ0sPi+PBNDeExMj\n=pgGp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T08:35:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gi