thub.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/commits/e74cebc38240317673d4e3a07f4d4f9bd976292b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:41:11Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:41:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0 (#1835)\n\n* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0\n\n2.0.0 restores @typescript-eslint/no-require-imports to error for source\nfiles, which 1.0.0 had disabled everywhere by mistake, and raises the\nconfig''s dependency floors to validated versions.\n\nThe config change requires two kinds of one-line fixes. Seven\neslint-disable comments for no-require-imports come back in the webpack,\nrspack, and storybook tooling packages. The ESLint 9 migration in #1827\nhad removed them as unused, which they only were because 1.0.0 had\nwrongly turned the rule off. Six stale testing-library directives go\naway, since eslint-plugin-testing-library moves from 7.1.1 to 7.16.2 and\nno longer reports at those sites.\n\nAll 30 workspaces lint green, with zero warnings under --max-warnings 0\nacross every lint surface including the storybook package''s .storybook\nand mocks directories.\n\n* Move the logout spec''s afterEach hook above the test\n\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1.0 to 2.11.0 with the config bump,\nand its prefer-hooks-on-top rule now warns when a hook follows test cases.\nA top-level afterEach applies to every test in the file wherever it is\ndeclared, so moving it above the test changes nothing at runtime and\nclears the warning that would otherwise block lint-staged commits\ntouching this file.","tree":{"sha":"c6e99db7bf54fa6d04f3edf12e1d0a57f1c6ba22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/trees/c6e99db7bf54fa6d04f3edf12e1d0a57f1c6ba22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/git/commits/e74cebc38240317673d4e3a07f4d4f9bd976292b","verification":{"payload":"tree c6e99db7bf54fa6d04f3edf12e1d0a57f1c6ba22\nparent d8a2f5b229323fdde21ac65705c6d7e8412b8566\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1785937271 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785937271 +0300\n\n(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0 (#1835)\n\n* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0\n\n2.0.0 restores @typescript-eslint/no-require-imports to error for source\nfiles, which 1.0.0 had disabled everywhere by mistake, and raises the\nconfig''s dependency floors to validated versions.\n\nThe config change requires two kinds of one-line fixes. Seven\neslint-disable comments for no-require-imports come back in the webpack,\nrspack, and storybook tooling packages. The ESLint 9 migration in #1827\nhad removed them as unused, which they only were because 1.0.0 had\nwrongly turned the rule off. Six stale testing-library directives go\naway, since eslint-plugin-testing-library moves from 7.1.1 to 7.16.2 and\nno longer reports at those sites.\n\nAll 30 workspaces lint green, with zero warnings under --max-warnings 0\nacross every lint surface including the storybook package''s .storybook\nand mocks directories.\n\n* Move the logout spec''s afterEach hook above the test\n\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1.0 to 2.11.0 with the config bump,\nand its prefer-hooks-on-top rule now warns when a hook follows test cases.\nA top-level afterEach applies to every test in the file wherever it is\ndeclared, so moving it above the test changes nothing at runtime and\nclears the warning that would otherwise block lint-staged commits\ntouching this file.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcz13CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5wcQACtDGCgwx+6dW0u78LQPF9J+\n5tkpTWUc/P/uO0/h5sgVX0sYavVeRvDhtWp21OXOwWBFykmaAnLwdlew4X5cYk8l\nFSXr0s+XiyTp+5oDSzfFZlP5a3DczLlj4vPSr4bQp33itqezSOu13Hm2p/K8PuCA\nW/VHRv57UtB0ganYUF6h9zVHKbGTdBKVwK0PcJOyRmbQK+SnP