roving published package subpaths and\ncaller-defined remotes resolve correctly through real rspack builds and\nVitest runs, independent of remote-map order. Document the issue #92\nevidence and project-level checks.\n\n## Why\n\nOverlapping specifiers must resolve to their own exported targets\nconsistently across production and tests; otherwise key reordering can\nsilently break the subpath-module architecture.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38dd9628a09926253b1ca966a27f51ef20cc76f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/38dd9628a09926253b1ca966a27f51ef20cc76f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/9d61608f90c295170708f199b9e739d5bdab78c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 38dd9628a09926253b1ca966a27f51ef20cc76f6\nparent d76803fadd5f0d5d63a9ebf889bc9d34bbf894ed\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1788066333 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788066333 +0000\n\nfix(testing): let a longer specifier resolve past the shorter alias it begins with (#99)\n\n## What\n\nAdd an executable contract proving published package subpaths and\ncaller-defined remotes resolve correctly through real rspack builds and\nVitest runs, independent of remote-map order. Document the issue #92\nevidence and project-level checks.\n\n## Why\n\nOverlapping specifiers must resolve to their own exported targets\nconsistently across production and tests; otherwise key reordering can\nsilently break the subpath-module architecture.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqk7odCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA82IQAFIBLt0rL5azJ4wtbtcOAqXu\naM71CnNl1rehmM9AlQ1cwd7h3C5y0B9w0iq2LEj4ezsqUu7eYv6jV8FOi