4ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/a5bd455065d506d0a9728ff6a48ad5e63c4045d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:05:22Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:05:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(ssr): record the TanStack Start evaluation and its recommendation (#94)\n\n## What\n\nAdd an evidence-backed decision record evaluating TanStack Start’s fit\nfor the current federated static-site architecture. It recommends\nagainst scheduling a migration today, identifies the repository\ninvariants that must remain intact, and defines the evidence and benefit\nthreshold that would justify revisiting that decision.\n\n## Why\n\nTanStack Start would replace some hand-built SSR and document assembly,\nbut adopting it is a thirteen-app build-system project rather than a\nframework swap. Recording the tradeoffs now makes the scheduling\ndecision durable without starting migration work or requiring the\nanalysis to be re-derived later.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8165312f4d3131a66a2469d5c83059f6061934bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/8165312f4d3131a66a2469d5c83059f6061934bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/a5bd455065d506d0a9728ff6a48ad5e63c4045d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 8165312f4d3131a66a2469d5c83059f6061934bc\nparent b9e0e26adbbb4c502778b6cd002d04a41a30c007\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1788051922 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788051922 +0000\n\ndocs(ssr): record the TanStack Start evaluation and its recommendation (#94)\n\n## What\n\nAdd an evidence-backed decision record evaluating TanStack Start’s fit\nfor the current federated static-site architecture. It recommends\nagainst scheduling a migration today, identifies the repository\ninvariants that must remain intact, and defines the evidence and benefit\nthreshold that would justify revisiting that decision.\n\n## Why\n\nTanStack Start would replace some hand-built SSR and document assembly,\nbut adopting it is a thirteen-app build-system project rather than a\nframework swap. Recording the tradeoffs now makes the scheduling\ndecision durable without starting migration work or requiring the\nanalysis to be re-derived later.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqk4HSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmaoQAKWgAYj45F8FY6dSIA4Qdfwl\nfJjTtleEeZuo0pbRtYuWtkUv1EkGFj8olfv6QWsyoEDfk/1nTFjZLMrdJxbMM391\nhs8GuhzQfGJdf+QU/mNPTbgfyaEFKQIkf6F+nC59WZjZur81tTYo8yjZbk4JiezC\nkYiPACIsw1g/L