l":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/6852f66fbaf110a008f1c8317119714eadf60327/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:53:29Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:53:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(publish-config): split the content-store publish path into its own library (#81)\n\n## What\n\nMoves the content-store publish path out of `build-config` into its own\n`publish-config` library, so the publish surface no longer sits on every\napp''s\ntypecheck path. A publish-path edit now selects the library that owns it\ninstead\nof thirteen app builds.\n\n- `libs/publish-config` owns `publish-fragment.ts`; the publish\nentrypoint is\n  resolved by alias at runtime.\n- Apps stop pulling every `build-config` source into their typechecks.\n- The remote registry reads through one validated view with a single\nschema.\n- `affected-build-projects.spec.ts` holds the new selection against the\nreal Nx\ngraph, including a separate assertion that no build-capable project\ndepends on\n`publish-config` — the `shell` is admitted only because `eslint .` reads\nevery\nTypeScript file, and that admission is stated against the graph rather\nthan\n  against one file''s selection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just gate` green over the finished tree (`NX_BASE=origin/master`).\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/master`: 39 rules, 14 passed, 0 failed.\n- Pre-push visual guard: all 12 microfrontends captured, all unchanged\nagainst\n  their committed baselines.\n\n`software`''s `standalone/loading/desktop` shot reported drift on one\nguard run.\nTwo fresh container captures both reproduced the committed hash\n`25b90785…` byte-for-byte and `screencomp classify` exits 0, so that was\na\ncapture flake; the committed baseline is unchanged and correct.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fbf8d694d74164a53c1c2f7d870b1d002a94876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/4fbf8d694d74164a53c1c2f7d870b1d002a94876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/6852f66fbaf110a008f1c8317119714eadf60327","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fbf8d694d74164a53c1c2f7d870b1d002a94876\nparent 52c20dc49778d8714c0292791647ea9ce1ef8eb8\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1786985609 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786985609 +0000\n\nrefactor(publish-config): split the content-store publish path into its own library (#81)\n\n## What\n\nMoves the content-store publish path out of `build-config` into its own\n`publish-config` library, so the publish surface no longer sits on every\napp''s\ntypecheck path. A publish-path edit now selects the library that owns it\ninstead\nof thirteen app builds.\n\n- `libs/publish-config` owns `publish-fragment.ts`; the publish\nentrypoint is\n  resolved by alias at runtime.\n- Apps stop pulling every `build-config` source into their typechecks.\n- The remote registry reads through one validated view with a single\nschema.\n- `affected-build-projects.spec.ts` holds the new selection against the\nreal Nx\ngraph, including a separate assertion that no build-capable project\ndepends on\n`publish-config` — the `shell` is admitted only because `eslint .` reads\nevery\nTypeScript file, and that admission is stated against the graph rather\nthan\n  against one file''s selection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just gate` green over the finished tree (`NX_BASE=origin/master`).\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/master`: 39 rules, 14 passed, 0 failed.\n- Pre-push visual guard: all 12 microfrontends captured, all unchanged\nagainst\n  their committed baselines.\n\n`software`''s `standalone/loading/desktop` shot reported drift on one\nguard run.\nTwo fresh container captures both reproduced the committed hash\n`25b90785…` byte-for-byte and `screencomp classify` exits 0, so that was\na\ncapture flake; the committed baseline is unchanged and correct.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgzyJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsDsQAB/yBlwo3U4mNCdhurePm4J3\n5qEg95iYL/Wd6c4YYCWcdibQtb8Kc+J4OikozxFXn/dX0BAyY6hSk1+jUuxuIUbz\n+elkd6DMp9LpwAvyht7jcGsrXyzoZd5KCVrJtslN9lHC4s9t+3yNZNkXeVR1XjUm\nOvYyPloIB6kme8Q9Lq2BQRvJvW7vwxLKPMI/vZRLk48zPQ0eP46orr0GqfjAc5V7\nXnJtouLZh5Ls8a9gicf7Fu01MTLWprATi4ouxMo44oktJisVfwhUBQ8A/cZVshfe\njNzuZocZY/PjcpNYYYgWJgsZiRN7qpEsu1OUoZbq5R/MA4Ta4uMPvL9xJBORzrek\niPuH7IT7QCTLrscMrE7Ug6ECLmtnGhqeMzWkxEB3ySOy4dkLwE2z9KEIVM32ikHW\nJYe4GLNvc8CfAhtxQSJaS5UHDVpstrRPezkhDY9Q2v3QJD4uXJL0ywr4rhgmgYsJ\nuyPRncPC6pgIC2DCaTjuwkfFqtsbOHjp/HsdvMt5NomiDd3GuW3Fst8MNJZV88Kx\nhOnA8OLNeWDiJ3yoq4HNYKSbvHmsXTctbP1AzPBaScZUvWiUSb8GHvvICU65nT/q\nPyN8cr7p0VZYAINukYbWdrc3QLIarA9nBm0Rjw6NKni7yJykBeO9+Zx57et8Frda\ndgSTsiyN/uh5zBamZHTW\n=bMFj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T16:53:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://