"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/52c20dc49778d8714c0292791647ea9ce1ef8eb8","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDUyYzIwZGM0OTc3OGQ4NzE0YzAyOTI3OTE2NDdlYTljZTFlZjhlYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893","sha":"c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893"}],"sha":"52c20dc49778d8714c0292791647ea9ce1ef8eb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/52c20dc49778d8714c0292791647ea9ce1ef8eb8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:09:13Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T12:09:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(workspace): enforce the per-app structure and coverage floor (#76)\n\n## What\n\nMakes the per-app testing structure self-enforcing and records it.\n\n- Adds a workspace contract test that derives its subjects from the real\nNx project graph and fails when the structure regresses: every app has a\n`vite.config.ts`, an `e2e/` directory, and — for projects with a\n`screenshot` target — a `visual/scenarios.ts`; no `test` target passes\n`--passWithNoTests`; coverage thresholds hold at 95 on all four metrics;\nevery component file has a co-located spec; every script, `just` recipe,\nand hook has a co-located spec.\n- Localizes the journey contract under the apps that own it, routes\nreviews for the localized instruction layers, and records why that layer\ncarries no CODEOWNERS.\n- Drops boundary directives the new test configs never needed, and\nnarrows the judge''s findings on the new specs.\n- Reaches each workflow-lint CLI through the command surface that owns\nit, and narrows the project paths the workspace contract reads from\ndisk.\n- Fixes the performance audit to audit each local route once rather than\nonce per scenario.\n\n## Why\n\nEvery preceding change established a convention that nothing enforced,\nso the next feature could silently reintroduce a component with no test,\na centralized suite, or a coverage `include` narrowed until its\nthreshold meant nothing. The enforcement test is what makes the\nconvention survive; the documentation is what lets the next contributor\nfollow it deliberately. The stale boundary and instruction-layer\ndirectives existed only because features could not previously be\nlocalized under individual apps — now that they can, those\njustifications no longer hold.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"832eaa86d007cdab10f4893b23ede16fbd0bac8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/832eaa86d007cdab10f4893b23ede16fbd0bac8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893","verification":{"payload":"tree 832eaa86d007cdab10f4893b23ede16fbd0bac8f\nparent 4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1786018153 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786018153 +0000\n\ntest(workspace): enforce the per-app structure and coverage floor (#76)\n\n## What\n\nMakes the per-app testing structure self-enforcing and records it.\n\n- Adds a workspace contract test that derives its subjects from the real\nNx project graph and fails when the structure regresses: every app has a\n`vite.config.ts`, an `e2e/` directory, and — for projects with a\n`screenshot` target — a `visual/scenarios.ts`; no `test` target passes\n`--passWithNoTests`; coverage thresholds hold at 95 on all four metrics;\nevery component file has a co-located spec; every script, `just` recipe,\nand hook has a co-located spec.\n- Localizes the journey contract under the apps that own it, routes\nreviews for the localized instruction layers, and records why that layer\ncarries no CODEOWNERS.\n- Drops boundary directives the new test configs never needed, and\nnarrows the judge''s findings on the new specs.\n- Reaches each workflow-lint CLI through the command surface that owns\nit, and narrows the project paths the workspace contract reads from\ndisk.\n- Fixes the performance audit to audit each local route once rather than\nonce per scenario.\n\n## Why\n\nEvery preceding change established a convention that nothing enforced,\nso the next feature could silently reintroduce a component with no test,\na centralized suite, or a coverage `include` narrowed until its\nthreshold meant nothing. The enforcement test is what makes the\nconvention survive; the documentation is what lets the next contributor\nfollow it deliberately. The stale boundary and instruction-layer\ndirectives existed only because features could not previously be\nlocalized under individual apps — now that they can, those\njustifications no longer hold.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdHlpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuZYQAAQuu47QBoMg8uyYrpyeV1YQ\nmqHEGPWzsbrQJ+WTsGT4tjkDfJZ15Zhti4KffbtZwW5KE7HMhC8s8+2tIqJvjojQ\nhZCdWUItulHhEtNNtQ0cSyObLk3anntcOShK9BQxsdA9u2I1DjhBXZFCcK0nNCBv\neRU+c0UQE9eDo2K2Ul52kD0rxkJNK/U+OrcED8MshxaUxszxpxFsskm1XMSGIRwE\ndua5GCG5wt4xGvjS1H+BM6bglwO9nLIYrINdu2yHVm7gdFMel/YzN2pUhIOF4GCd\nLKcqs+NGmtciErKOiYRwoKdsNKs2BTmV072PBYlj9e0jYPabuXX+nzeWHSC22y1p\nvSxu+VRFunjmUAjKjIuR7bGcPZbj0nKuYmXEqFkOwcYdaQWBAinfM1nUzR9S92Jj\nN5nTG5TQMCUBqCONwKbfc1HR6uHU0LkMhErKVdjep9YhbRNq3mn4D/P5CKB72P9K\nDoPp4Om3B/pS5SjDqbXK4nubgPFw7U/0IKzyiJ/KNZrEKBMzRgH6ALzc0VzbwmTD\nH/x6vdSE9JQ85Z554lr2d45qPNvdu9UEgGHV5yNCxho1MCp6rDYcCqRH7UHvdXF2\nVHFNBGG3xZMusmPJS6oxx3pbFihBXGkg+uaPEzTgG1/hdLM92d0tlgDhowS8TQuY\n6CguZzVNRQy1ugo00Au6\n=Sq2x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T12:18:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKGM4NDA3YjFiOThhMDgxZGZkZGQyNTgyY2QzNzNkYmQ4NjYxODU4OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45","sha":"4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45"}],"sha":"c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/c8407b1b98a081dfddd2582cd373dbd866185893"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:33:02Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:33:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(home): component suites and coverage floor for the home host and its panes (#73)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `home`, `home-cards`, `home-carousel`, `home-contact`, and\n`home-story` onto the pattern proven by `apps/awards`.\n\n- Splits each app so every component owns its file, including pulling\nHome''s pane wiring out of `page.tsx` and each pane app''s state component\nout of its page.\n- Adds a co-located spec beside every component, hook, and skeleton.\n- Wires each app''s `vite.config.ts` through `defineAppTestConfig` and\nreplaces `--passWithNoTests` with a real coverage run at the 95%\nfour-metric floor.\n- Covers Home through both render paths, resolving its federation\nspecifiers to the sibling apps'' real sources rather than stubs.\n- Records the narrow-viewport baselines for the home apps.\n\n## Why\n\nThese five apps had no component tests at all, and Home is the nested\nfederation host whose composition of the other four was proven only\nthrough a browser journey. Component-level coverage of the host''s pane\nwiring catches the class of break that previously surfaced only after a\nfull thirteen-app build.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7de93e7e4feb06a9c2913dec8a4e0a7244797343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/7de93e7e4feb06a9c2913dec8a4e0a7244797343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45","verification":{"payload":"tree 7de93e7e4feb06a9c2913dec8a4e0a7244797343\nparent 1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785987182 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785987182 +0000\n\ntest(home): component suites and coverage floor for the home host and its panes (#73)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `home`, `home-cards`, `home-carousel`, `home-contact`, and\n`home-story` onto the pattern proven by `apps/awards`.\n\n- Splits each app so every component owns its file, including pulling\nHome''s pane wiring out of `page.tsx` and each pane app''s state component\nout of its page.\n- Adds a co-located spec beside every component, hook, and skeleton.\n- Wires each app''s `vite.config.ts` through `defineAppTestConfig` and\nreplaces `--passWithNoTests` with a real coverage run at the 95%\nfour-metric floor.\n- Covers Home through both render paths, resolving its federation\nspecifiers to the sibling apps'' real sources rather than stubs.\n- Records the narrow-viewport baselines for the home apps.\n\n## Why\n\nThese five apps had no component tests at all, and Home is the nested\nfederation host whose composition of the other four was proven only\nthrough a browser journey. Component-level coverage of the host''s pane\nwiring catches the class of break that previously surfaced only after a\nfull thirteen-app build.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdABuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL8EQAGHnvtYdHQQMCFATUqo84Sv+\nKR/iukUwgAgPfBw1dgmVpm1D/kCH9Db3VbqJ/JC1ZrjhMDZ60VRRgK4Y3S2BSqn3\nefpWZd+HnjGdPvmPh5AA7xmqcPskWQi8dczbprjI6G6/Krlj/etB97lFde7e49TL\nuB2GlGeSPjUgLUS13H9H7uCX4YxETKRkGrPVyUJZ/8IRgixXw8XB5uVTDl/+c6tp\naFSNLTeLdDaAwwmRTNJkLbG2QkGI7I8VdU5OtdTYDlAejd5Ei6Ozn132DzNpnmRz\nWHbW+esrJnwn/tGagAmlhc9cErEkGbDpMM6o9ONggghnTmXAf49tD8gD+QGMxHPk\nCLUwRLdIDbY5zbc3vHy54onLN8sCaPzUAEOWkksua8Injv2QSSvuWbfBtR5OX1WO\nDCiVyEQsH8bfbU14wbZ2n2G0AmklgzqbtZNQUyAePaXjLPu1/7fadr/WFO/wcdlt\nWIsfKQpu/CDAw3+1tDkWGHpuZsNSWab0A28XrU+bGLxHmmmZusmu0mbhO+vEgQmr\nXDnsajBLRacybXvOBbdJ+rraR3n1J9bqxSNKwYIIOgzlON/rgp3oXUQYPZS9Bydq\nYhAZuzdQtSzjHnhy5EpWUfP5zpFlmBbGcx9GKp5IUm+YdvmiOwVKY46EgyajRfxr\noKiv0f2QcQUFifCMQTSK\n=p+sq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T03:33:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDRlNGI0MTg5MzNhMWFiZjNlM2U1ODBiNmY3MjQyOGU0YjE4YzZmNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765","sha":"1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765"}],"sha":"4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/4e4b418933a1abf3e3e580b6f72428e4b18c6f45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:19:01Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:19:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(shell): component suites for skills, timeline, and the shell (#74)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `skills`, `timeline`, and `shell` — the three heaviest source\nfiles in the workspace — onto the pattern proven by `apps/awards`.\n\n- **skills**: `page.tsx` (267 lines) split into `chart`,\n`chart-controls`, `chart-geometry`, `dropdowns`, `skill-details`,\n`skills-experience`, `skills-state`, `preview-state`, plus the\n`use-chart-model` and `use-dropdown-model` hooks, each with a co-located\nspec. The drill-down is asserted from both the pointer and the keyboard.\n- **timeline**: one component per file with a co-located spec suite.\n- **shell**: the router measured and split one component per file;\ncoverage widened past `routes.ts`; every loaded route''s\nunusable-CV-domain recovery driven in a real browser.\n- Registers and captures the new skills and timeline visual states a\nvisitor can reach.\n- Drops an ineffective lint suppression.\n\n## Why\n\nSkills and timeline hold the workspace''s most interactive markup and had\nno component tests at all. The shell had a 95% threshold, but its\ncoverage `include` named only `routes.ts` — so the 362-line router\nowning every route transition, the 404 recovery, and the `/story`\nredirect had never been measured. The threshold read as enforced while\nthe code it should govern was scoped out of it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c4f1e573e375bb08890f7e0c3b10e64cb59665ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/c4f1e573e375bb08890f7e0c3b10e64cb59665ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765","verification":{"payload":"tree c4f1e573e375bb08890f7e0c3b10e64cb59665ef\nparent 1c6213b85aad4af4036bf13a25752d7f505f7f1f\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785986341 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785986341 +0000\n\ntest(shell): component suites for skills, timeline, and the shell (#74)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `skills`, `timeline`, and `shell` — the three heaviest source\nfiles in the workspace — onto the pattern proven by `apps/awards`.\n\n- **skills**: `page.tsx` (267 lines) split into `chart`,\n`chart-controls`, `chart-geometry`, `dropdowns`, `skill-details`,\n`skills-experience`, `skills-state`, `preview-state`, plus the\n`use-chart-model` and `use-dropdown-model` hooks, each with a co-located\nspec. The drill-down is asserted from both the pointer and the keyboard.\n- **timeline**: one component per file with a co-located spec suite.\n- **shell**: the router measured and split one component per file;\ncoverage widened past `routes.ts`; every loaded route''s\nunusable-CV-domain recovery driven in a real browser.\n- Registers and captures the new skills and timeline visual states a\nvisitor can reach.\n- Drops an ineffective lint suppression.\n\n## Why\n\nSkills and timeline hold the workspace''s most interactive markup and had\nno component tests at all. The shell had a 95% threshold, but its\ncoverage `include` named only `routes.ts` — so the 362-line router\nowning every route transition, the 404 recovery, and the `/story`\nredirect had never been measured. The threshold read as enforced while\nthe code it should govern was scoped out of it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc/0lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaPUQAFWPLm0l4HgcAV6vbbhNSk5h\n7F/3OzoNErjL9PlrSsTYe7jDIx0e1rFJa0Yc/SMDYYKYTILJK4YYoi/1BwZ5PWpx\nCTLn4ZlOC6S2uh7Yr5lmjwX6PnQY1lbFvOtHKTU+JMU604Lf+C0w5haIGSF4G+0W\ncWhIKKp9Xd+WTTTT0Pq/rYwiWXXuKWICb+X64gOa24yc2XfeEYdfhQpmjYztGsKX\nw63RzOcBP4vZQTyzFSo2yb/ZaFnZj7hWV+vUWUAJa8ckyamw4Gamw