bc592ec00f63f765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/1ab12a772ab90e19a767baa5bc592ec00f63f765"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/1c6213b85aad4af4036bf13a25752d7f505f7f1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:09:51Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T03:09:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(routes): component suites and coverage floors for bio, courses, research, and software (#75)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `bio`, `courses`, `research`, and `software` onto the pattern\nproven by `apps/awards`.\n\n- Splits every file holding more than one component so each owns its\nfile — `bio` into `marker`, `biography`, `bio-state`, `page`; `courses`\ninto `resource-tree`, `course-details`, `course-pane` and friends;\nlikewise `research` and `software`.\n- Adds a co-located spec beside every component, hook, and skeleton.\n- Wires each app''s `vite.config.ts` through `defineAppTestConfig` and\nreplaces `--passWithNoTests` with a real coverage run at the 95%\nfour-metric floor.\n- Regenerates the four data-driven routes'' visual baselines.\n- Settles each entry''s lazy page before asserting on it, and names the\nspec helpers for what they look up.\n\n## Why\n\nThese four are the data-driven route remotes and had no component tests\nat all. Their empty, loading, and error branches are reachable by any\nvisitor whenever the CV data fetch degrades, and nothing proved those\nbranches rendered correctly except a browser journey that had to build\nall thirteen apps first.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"890e0bea07b529ebf911b07c23110b8209236182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/890e0bea07b529ebf911b07c23110b8209236182"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/1c6213b85aad4af4036bf13a25752d7f505f7f1f","verification":{"payload":"tree 890e0bea07b529ebf911b07c23110b8209236182\nparent 0f1e4c21e0fb216945382c94271ed4ea95f37e4c\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785985791 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785985791 +0000\n\ntest(routes): component suites and coverage floors for bio, courses, research, and software (#75)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `bio`, `courses`, `research`, and `software` onto the pattern\nproven by `apps/awards`.\n\n- Splits every file holding more than one component so each owns its\nfile — `bio` into `marker`, `biography`, `bio-state`, `page`; `courses`\ninto `resource-tree`, `course-details`, `course-pane` and friends;\nlikewise `research` and `software`.\n- Adds a co-located spec beside every component, hook, and skeleton.\n- Wires each app''s `vite.config.ts` through `defineAppTestConfig` and\nreplaces `--passWithNoTests` with a real coverage run at the 95%\nfour-metric floor.\n- Regenerates the four data-driven routes'' visual baselines.\n- Settles each entry''s lazy page before asserting on it, and names the\nspec helpers for what they look up.\n\n## Why\n\nThese four are the data-driven route remotes and had no component tests\nat all. Their empty, loading, and error branches are reachable by any\nvisitor whenever the CV data fetch degrades, and nothing proved those\nbranches rendered correctly except a browser journey that had to build\nall thirteen apps first.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc/r/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0mcQABoUv3guXq9qCiXxdmzPMSTs\nBGTkQYyFw5SEsP86GseB8HIMdNcHEOReBzIKOz7H/iGjem42r8rACc5wmuOuk+FF\n282USTc2gA5m7TSM87JOzcqnKxAnffp889YU6no06Blo+cjXWAMWAQx7Ujgl/RoO\ntKj0qc8ny+voXiQFvO4+lhR8ehEvUIJcsg/CBb43VK+QsfTPu5QyPLBdIG8G9Hm2\nIokGGcP1Nc4XBVwccon6NcbJIK0mo2BUudF1C7edo/FREO8aaZFaMQaVoVgfI72O\navbc+erae2e6yU++v5+RzGY7Jqp9uYxTyPeCFRnJeQzTtXQHgwziwzh8Z9b5Uy0B\nFblRPXKJBaMqC7QDB1yVl3wxlzKxiv0OX4LY0dOj8xgQ9xOARxAamDQ/jMBbmztO\nINPKrJUjIg45mjmMa6CbV2hzZ3FXCDwKzfI0pZVHTy5Ww8BsAGBH90dKQzEnD1ym\nWb1H8qvj8ewdVC53Nt2450lFOXdpvaTigBwgxA/GKs3ANyrpjXliSiftFpYNUaVN\nA8DIZcCsb2xYYVpkl4K11scW7jkxmdNw/Lq1ImKhc1F5UoUX/sqta0K5iqycCLvu\nilF9orqvvcx3k/hdRx0UAIstB+gaYuA+kWy461y40JbTMElHSsM2uGJR5K95F2Ac\nWcnmAiYZrmYK9XXOcX/s\n=+8Ri\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T03:10:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/1c6213b85aad4af4036bf13a25752d7f505f7f1f","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDFjNjIxM2I4NWFhZDRhZjQwMzZiZjEzYTI1NzUyZDdmNTA1ZjdmMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/0f1e4c21e0fb216945382c94271ed4ea95f37e4c","sha":"0f1e4c21e0fb216945382c94271ed4ea95f37e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/0f1e4c21e0fb216945382c94271ed4ea95f37e4c"}],"sha":"1c6213b85aad4af4036bf13a25752d7f505f7f1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/1c6213b85aad4af4036bf13a25752d7f505f7f1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/0f1e4c21e0fb216945382c94271ed4ea95f37e4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T23:35:57Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T23:35:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(awards): component suite, coverage floor, and every reachable visual state (#72)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `apps/awards` fully onto the merged harnesses as the worked\nexample for the remaining twelve apps.\n\n- Splits `page.tsx` and `award-emblem.tsx` so each component owns its\nfile: `award-card`, `award-emblem`, `award-icon`, `awards-state`,\n`awards-statistics`, `laurel-branch`, `page`, `skeleton`, plus the\n`use-awards` hook.\n- Adds a co-located spec beside every component, hook, and skeleton.\n- Wires `apps/awards/vite.config.ts` through `defineAppTestConfig` and\nreplaces the `--passWithNoTests` target with a real coverage run at the\n95% four-metric floor.\n- Extends `apps/awards/visual/scenarios.ts` to capture every reachable\npane state at every viewport, including the phone-viewport boundary\nstates, and regenerates the baseline.\n- Locks both directions of the remote''s hydration guard.\n\n## Why\n\nThe twelve remote apps had zero component tests — every `test` target\nwas `vitest run --passWithNoTests` with no spec files — so the 95% floor\nthe libraries already met had never applied to any UI. Proving the\npattern on one app first means the remaining twelve follow a worked\nexample rather than twelve independent interpretations of it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1972591470c36a4a4abd8b6fe959579d8820e70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/d1972591470c36a4a4abd8b6fe959579d8820e70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/0f1e4c21e0fb216945382c94271ed4ea95f37e4c","verification":{"payload":"tree d1972591470c36a4a4abd8b6fe959579d8820e70\nparent ebf8db05a1e5a35fbfcbc9945b15f93c07e97836\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785972957 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785972957 +0000\n\ntest(awards): component suite, coverage floor, and every reachable visual state (#72)\n\n## What\n\nBrings `apps/awards` fully onto the merged harnesses as the worked\nexample for the remaining twelve apps.\n\n- Splits `page.tsx` and `award-emblem.tsx` so each component owns its\nfile: `award-card`, `award-emblem`, `award-icon`, `awards-state`,\n`awards-statistics`, `laurel-branch`, `page`, `skeleton`, plus the\n`use-awards` hook.\n- Adds a co-located spec beside every component, hook, and skeleton.\n- Wires `apps/awards/vite.config.ts` through `defineAppTestConfig` and\nreplaces the `--passWithNoTests` target with a real coverage run at the\n95% four-metric floor.\n- Extends `apps/awards/visual/scenarios.ts` to capture every reachable\npane state at every viewport, including the phone-viewport boundary\nstates, and regenerates the baseline.\n- Locks both directions of the remote''s hydration guard.\n\n## Why\n\nThe twelve remote apps had zero component tests — every `test` target\nwas `vitest run --passWithNoTests` with no spec files — so the 95% floor\nthe libraries already met had never applied to any UI. Proving the\npattern on one app first means the remaining twelve follow a worked\nexample rather than twelve independent interpretations of it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <