/L5KcgwnZGSe4l15oUhROeinfmF20pPX3s2K5mKB+1XhOPf51PU5NMMe+t\nDgxOqOwtNWgChV9SagwcYQ1F3lHuev4rl2udHIZDxRiIXIKTd+kT8NZclPpq3b29\n4u86+hnRT6WrKo3GKqgpcvfIK6kiz9Tb+HdrtbK36iqlSygIUleebhqndhOso4/t\nZRk+LvaGmHwoOu12a8sFfI7KPYrr4/uVDFzvi9HOpgZrO7xX1df68xldRaUjUdVN\nanAIN98tNRgdLQIB4Lf7/3A2+otznJ7U9ZpziL2/wgjuBi0bxyxdt7W6XPsAQEnP\nNmC8QZayJ3/a4pfC33nF\n=KsEm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T22:36:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/fb65ec433be644ec90136d23cf017945613f8cdb","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKGZiNjVlYzQzM2JlNjQ0ZWM5MDEzNmQyM2NmMDE3OTQ1NjEzZjhjZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015","sha":"823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015"}],"sha":"fb65ec433be644ec90136d23cf017945613f8cdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/fb65ec433be644ec90136d23cf017945613f8cdb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:22:49Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:22:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(compose): stage the shell''s bundle into the artifact and gate its references (#68)\n\n`just compose <store>/apps <output>` wrote route documents, `404.html`,\n`cv-data/`, and `remotes/<name>/` but never staged the shell''s own\npublished\nbytes, so every composed document referenced a `runtime.<hash>.js`,\n`main.<hash>.js`, `main.<hash>.css`, and `remoteEntry.js` that nothing\nput in\nthe artifact. That was invisible while the output defaulted to the\nshell''s own\nbuild directory; the deploy lane composes into a fresh `dist/site`, so\nthe\ndeployed site served prerendered markup and 404ed every script and\nstylesheet.\n\nCompose now stages each app''s published bytes verbatim, withholding only\n`fragment.html`, `fragment.css`, and `fragment.json` — its own inputs,\nwhich no\nbrowser requests — and, for the shell subtree, the entries compose\nwrites at\nthe artifact root, so a shell published from a tree that composed into\nits own\nbuild directory cannot restore a stale composition.\n\n`check-static-artifact.mjs` now resolves every `<script src>` and\n`<link rel=\"stylesheet\">` in every composed document the way a browser\ndoes,\nthrough the document''s `<base href>` and the Pages base path, and\nrefuses an\nartifact that references bytes it does not contain.\n\ncomposed-artifact.spec.ts drives the CI topology the existing journeys\ncannot:\nit composes a content-store-shaped fragment root into a fresh directory,\nserves\nthat directory as Pages does, and asserts no failed request across every\nroute,\na client-side navigation, and every standalone remote document.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13099e4b9e7137123229c1a7c6c7e39e93fcc9f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/13099e4b9e7137123229c1a7c6c7e39e93fcc9f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015","verification":{"payload":"tree 13099e4b9e7137123229c1a7c6c7e39e93fcc9f7\nparent 34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785774169 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785774169 +0000\n\nfix(compose): stage the shell''s bundle into the artifact and gate its references (#68)\n\n`just compose <store>/apps <output>` wrote route documents, `404.html`,\n`cv-data/`, and `remotes/<name>/` but never staged the shell''s own\npublished\nbytes, so every composed document referenced a `runtime.<hash>.js`,\n`main.<hash>.js`, `main.<hash>.css`, and `remoteEntry.js` that nothing\nput in\nthe artifact. That was invisible while the output defaulted to the\nshell''s own\nbuild directory; the deploy lane composes into a fresh `dist/site`, so\nthe\ndeployed site served prerendered markup and 404ed every script and\nstylesheet.\n\nCompose now stages each app''s published bytes verbatim, withholding only\n`fragment.html`, `fragment.css`, and `fragment.json` — its own inputs,\nwhich no\nbrowser requests — and, for the shell subtree, the entries compose\nwrites at\nthe artifact root, so a shell published from a tree that composed into\nits own\nbuild directory cannot restore a stale composition.\n\n`check-static-artifact.mjs` now resolves every `<script src>` and\n`<link rel=\"stylesheet\">` in every composed document the way a browser\ndoes,\nthrough the document''s `<base href>` and the Pages base path, and\nrefuses an\nartifact that references bytes it does not contain.\n\ncomposed-artifact.spec.ts drives the CI topology the existing journeys\ncannot:\nit composes a content-store-shaped fragment root into a fresh directory,\nserves\nthat directory as Pages does, and asserts no failed request across every\nroute,\na client-side navigation, and every standalone remote document.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcMBZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAtYQAKNqzNBrFHpHsmKAlatJVrJa\nA6ngIAFp9CAoM8eF1lQOA5upLda4fXbJoisAswsimiWpSb47QID32a5mQkI3fr6x\nH7GbHeXcMIzKXSN9mQ/vD1eVqptqkbOnVlsa96Wa6yPabjOuWDipw9DOv+bpzqZI\ngLuDeuiGeBNBrXXZvXKFrOd3Taga2Cl7pFo8qpgfDQoveH9zyFukNStFO0zMXX5r\n+tHydebPhb84/VqD44x/gfz/mG+xIr8ycxvaXMlBtmkxk6PvH3IiGVJx6Q25kCrc\n2uyKxoGVxTTYV0UDANAdVqjhi4lwvyOi6aFjBPYB0B9KQEp3+Yox8C2g2u4Ct7X1\nJTHRNpl2iTIRarhiMTFcgTTQj57KD2lE5QMi7SZzyTHgjV86I2q/YuJatKO5/bc8\n3v9Fxki7gkJZLnfGC/vdX9HziuWgGtX6wpHrqQ51ibNct/ezhLACJDawHcKVqxp6\nMLwOjLO9jWWLyVpEiZgl26TojaOKOCjWqPBLf0bVK3ofkB/1D418RdMb6MmKVKTp\nShrUZpeNudyr7sCywxf7fmu43SBiIuqvTwrkviVySqmFbDkHIqEn6YvtR21jy7qz\nAi9Y6SuXU8nn/MAujezKvMyoCe5dfPwEWD2tFyK9RTe6QuUtp8iCK4CjN4VLXCvr\nHLGZnsGcSWyehhMlfE7Q\n=ub4p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T16:23:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDgyMzg3NGM1MGJlMDFiOWIxZGQ0N2M3MTRmOTcwOWM5OTJkNTYwMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072","sha":"34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072"}],"sha":"823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/823874c50be01b9b1dd47c714f9709c992d56015"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T04:31:24Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T04:31:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: never refuse a push without saying why (#67)\n\n## What\nLand [PR\n#66](https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/pull/66).\nOne llmlint\nfinding remains, and the planner has decided it is a justified\nsuppression rather than a\ndefect to fix:\n\n    FAIL e2e_not_mocked\n      rationale: The Docker-unavailable case injects a PATH shim via\ndockerUnavailableFixture() instead of using the real Docker subprocess.\n      apps/shell-e2e/src/unit/visual-guard-hook.spec.ts:222\n\nAdd a narrow, site-scoped `ignore` directive at that site. Its\njustification must say what\nis actually true: the test''s subject *is* the absence of Docker, and\nthat condition cannot\nbe produced with a real Docker subprocess on a host where Docker is\ninstalled — the shim\nis the condition under test, not a stand-in that avoids a boundary. Note\nthat the guard''s\nDocker-available path is exercised for real elsewhere, if that is so; if\nit is not, say so\nrather than implying it.\n\nMatch the register of the existing `ignore-block[e2e_not_mocked]`\njustification in\n`apps/shell-e2e/src/unit/lint-llm-diff.spec.ts`, which is this\nrepository''s precedent for\nthe same rule.\n\nScope the directive as tightly as the rule allows — the single case, not\nthe file, unless\nthe rule cannot express that. Do not edit `llmlint.yml`. Do not suppress\nany other finding:\nthe other four are fixed and must stay fixed.\n\n## Why\n`llmlint` is a required check, and this one finding is all that stands\nbetween a finished\nchange and `master`. The change stops the pre-push visual guard from\nrefusing a push while\nprinting nothing, and fixes a silent false negative where an Nx\nproject-list parse failure\nread as \"no microfrontend was affected\" and let a push through — a guard\nthat passes on its\nown error is not guarding anything.\n\nThe rule is right in general and wrong here, which is exactly what a\nsite-scoped directive\nwith a real reason exists for. Suppressing it without that reason would\nbe the failure the\nrule is guarding against.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"58adcf34cdd680a5a593010de7b20922d88c434e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/58adcf34cdd680a5a593010de7b20922d88c434e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072","verification":{"payload":"tree 58adcf34cdd680a5a593010de7b20922d88c434e\nparent 7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785731484 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785731484 +0000\n\nfix: never refuse a push without saying why (#67)\n\n## What\nLand [PR\n#66](https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/pull/66).\nOne llmlint\nfinding remains, and the planner has decided it is a justified\nsuppression rather than a\ndefect to fix:\n\n    FAIL e2e_not_mocked\n      rationale: The Docker-unavailable case injects a PATH shim via\ndockerUnavailableFixture() instead of using the real Docker subprocess.\n      apps/shell-e2e/src/unit/visual-guard-hook.spec.ts:222\n\nAdd a narrow, site-scoped `ignore` directive at that site. Its\njustification must say what\nis actually true: the test''s subject *is* the absence of Docker, and\nthat condition cannot\nbe produced with a real Docker subprocess on a host where Docker is\ninstalled — the shim\nis the condition under test, not a stand-in that avoids a boundary. Note\nthat the guard''s\nDocker-available path is exercised for real elsewhere, if that is so; if\nit is not, say so\nrather than implying it.\n\nMatch the register of the existing `ignore-block[e2e_not_mocked]`\njustification in\n`apps/shell-e2e/src/unit/lint-llm-diff.spec.ts`, which is this\nrepository''s precedent for\nthe same rule.\n\nScope the directive as tightly as the rule allows — the single case, not\nthe file, unless\nthe rule cannot express that. Do not edit `llmlint.yml`. Do not suppress\nany other finding:\nthe other four are fixed and must stay fixed.\n\n## Why\n`llmlint` is a required check, and this one finding is all that stands\nbetween a finished\nchange and `master`. The change stops the pre-push visual guard from\nrefusing a push while\nprinting nothing, and fixes a silent false negative where an Nx\nproject-list parse failure\nread as \"no microfrontend was affected\" and let a push through — a guard\nthat passes on its\nown error is not guarding anything.\n\nThe rule is right in general and wrong here, which is exactly what a\nsite-scoped directive\nwith a real reason exists for. Suppressing it without that reason would\nbe the failure the\nrule is guarding against.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcBmcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaKsQAC4aXzbfLwKilBAlCjv8Z5TP\nJQiR29oO7xSAu4QLZfYMAmlt2R1L6Hf6UaZu3vhQ9knc4AlFRPRYTqo3nIfVGAUU\nVXDk086H08WHdOUZNJ4/VOJ252VXHideIC2haIXn9q9UV0ftN7gRmgSEnO//ZULS\nAIOEDQgkXI5HyzgCC14P3uAT4CZQ+82fIjejrWm+P63S7R2me/Ekq4VLQWCYI1d/\n75FyDOB//t2Rm4DWHdXOhuiaVMFGK1cMxJvloSULrlJmd3zAczceD74MMjHC9uJ+\n/pdix0Qa8F1JKCxTqULOlJ24UozSrLG6fhqzoLiL8zVx2lLDjt8nq/S77qWG5HgB\ne9hKARpnKqPHPMsuXLTCZtyAVGli48cO++hRSoVn8nUmNKx73GsmcmFGYRRqukpX\nZIY7kxccs2btclySYxvDLFhaO1X+uMeZGfJJ4Uw2X91nUugyfqWUMEXFyfHGCcz/\nOwQUKrRhdsfL7I4WP7oLNOollKmz/UgOK7hnnr0OfWdfq2hLmQ8MhjiXFE6j/3v7\n/jEbSI4Y38g6mOnHKrSYhphHBZPXlPBMUNGELyX7htdul3ECe/MjEMAofrDTYoka\nNaW2RvUfEHShNGRli3UYhgzkMT39Zy8sPntG8nnyqcITizBIoyRitznZp0OOUNaw\n5wY8pCoqeC2OZnQH9BVW\n=FhIQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T04:31:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDM0ZWU0MTZlNTEyZTg3NjZhYTlmMDEyZmZiZGM5NWRjZTg4YzEwNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37","sha":"7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37"}],"sha":"34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/34ee416e512e8766aa9f012ffbdc95dce88c1072"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T04:19:50Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T04:19:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(hooks): never refuse a push without saying why (#66)\n\n## What\nFinish and publish the change already committed on this branch.\n\n`e89a445 fix(hooks): never refuse a push without saying why` is complete\nwork: the\npre-push visual guard no longer dies inside the `pnpm exec nx show\nprojects` command\nsubstitution under `set -euo pipefail`. Every non-verdict exit now goes\nthrough one of two\nannouncements — a loud skip when the guard could not evaluate the push\nat all (matching\nthe existing `screencomp`-not-on-PATH branch, escalatable with\n`SCREENCOMP_GUARD_REQUIRE=1`), and a loud refusal when it evaluated and\ncould not clear.\nOnly an evaluated pass stays quiet. Its audit also fixed a silent\n**false negative**: an\nNx project-list parse failure previously read as \"no microfrontend was\naffected\" and let\nthe push through.\n\nThe previous dispatch died mid-gate when its provider hit a weekly quota\nlimit, not\nbecause anything was wrong with the change. Your job is to confirm it\nholds, run the\nrepository''s gate, and let the lifecycle publish it.\n\nVerify the guard by **running it**, not by reading it:\n\n- A clone with no workspace install must produce a clear diagnostic and\nskip, rather than\nexiting silently. Reproduce the original failure shape and show it is\ngone.\n- A run that can evaluate must still evaluate, and must still block on\ngenuine visual\n  drift. This change must not weaken the guard into a no-op.\n\nIf the gate demands fixes, make them. Otherwise do not rewrite the\nchange, do not amend\nits message beyond what a fix requires, and do not widen scope.\n\n## Why\nA pre-push guard that refuses a push while printing nothing is worse\nthan no guard: the\none layer that knows why is the one that stays silent, and every layer\nabove it can only\nreport `failed to push some refs`. That exact silence turned a small\ndiagnosis into hours\nof hand-tracing a hook with `bash -x`, across three tools that each\nfaithfully reported a\nbare push failure. The false-negative path matters more: a visual guard\nthat passes a push\nbecause it failed to parse its own input is not guarding anything, and\nnobody would know.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"58adcf34cdd680a5a593010de7b20922d88c434e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/58adcf34cdd680a5a593010de7b20922d88c434e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37","verification":{"payload":"tree 58adcf34cdd680a5a593010de7b20922d88c434e\nparent 57210a09be5bbd38e4334ec4feda5e03a92a1e7a\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785730790 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785730790 +0000\n\nfix(hooks): never refuse a push without saying why (#66)\n\n## What\nFinish and publish the change already committed on this branch.\n\n`e89a445 fix(hooks): never refuse a push without saying why` is complete\nwork: the\npre-push visual guard no longer dies inside the `pnpm exec nx show\nprojects` command\nsubstitution under `set -euo pipefail`. Every non-verdict exit now goes\nthrough one of two\nannouncements — a loud skip when the guard could not evaluate the push\nat all (matching\nthe existing `screencomp`-not-on-PATH branch, escalatable with\n`SCREENCOMP_GUARD_REQUIRE=1`), and a loud refusal when it evaluated and\ncould not clear.\nOnly an evaluated pass stays quiet. Its audit also fixed a silent\n**false negative**: an\nNx project-list parse failure previously read as \"no microfrontend was\naffected\" and let\nthe push through.\n\nThe previous dispatch died mid-gate when its provider hit a weekly quota\nlimit, not\nbecause anything was wrong with the change. Your job is to confirm it\nholds, run the\nrepository''s gate, and let the lifecycle publish it.\n\nVerify the guard by **running it**, not by reading it:\n\n- A clone with no workspace install must produce a clear diagnostic and\nskip, rather than\nexiting silently. Reproduce the original failure shape and show it is\ngone.\n- A run that can evaluate must still evaluate, and must still block on\ngenuine visual\n  drift. This change must not weaken the guard into a no-op.\n\nIf the gate demands fixes, make them. Otherwise do not rewrite the\nchange, do not amend\nits message beyond what a fix requires, and do not widen scope.\n\n## Why\nA pre-push guard that refuses a push while printing nothing is worse\nthan no guard: the\none layer that knows why is the one that stays silent, and every layer\nabove it can only\nreport `failed to push some refs`. That exact silence turned a small\ndiagnosis into hours\nof hand-tracing a hook with `bash -x`, across three tools that each\nfaithfully reported a\nbare push failure. The false-negative path matters more: a visual guard\nthat passes a push\nbecause it failed to parse its own input is not guarding anything, and\nnobody would know.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcBbmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARkoQACQRFR4JXrhLSXP9RPIpmlA4\nl++L4yqlHdmvjza48YEHLSE1Rl/68lfdAG+FJ7J1kWdQBmynR/gCi+urafyBCUc1\nSryMos4N2UvO4EL0G0kg7wl72OCDs/Bu7WsIb3CSNL9yqA2J5viUkJKLlfEFNnqa\nlj7TBo16lPPHKuMwVSw+mLjKPCMukZZcdJkxeZU1nU29whZhU3dvzp0zo+0RxiQP\nVc97ZGLpGCeAfN6prUQcBVd3IyAdl1gV1/8kEK3ZkYClFxZLOM6kQ/zHh6mVnNfL\nHwCDOFicPB8jYyJ1uxx8mhs0GyrN7R1dskvnt37doh/ea9OCZcw7Y0iAzI5xpO5D\n9uQYsv3yjYshr5KL3FBe4P7jqNMvdkB2L2gJ96Atm46oOvGxFZd6GjUGOzOtLaE/\nSPIMPlk4X3SFFUcbcsaC+Z8AZDMS0vLCfY0g4o6k2GHSACfjSUMJ7hUjMf2WjmSF\njWFyyAWIbNF0Hqcxdw90C1lewVhsGLeFwt93puf7gRRknW98fxUpLNSyQNyykigF\nz7sS/3vge3s8dYosYE4CF5kqOdPqn5X3xQpULgrBscavqo4gP0BLaHYGlUGCzAYW\nSop2xmG1CZQdvH4qs76RTwqRmALEpfC4GeqotIJA1Zl920Z+u7Z9u+PSXGKe/7zS\nmgxyCC2PRCLuCKqRdGFS\n=oO8i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T04:19:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDdmNTAwNjQ1ZDE1OGU5MjhlZTVjOGJmMjNiNzMxNDdkNDdjMjVlMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/57210a09be5bbd38e4334ec4feda5e03a92a1e7a","sha":"57210a09be5bbd38e4334ec4feda5e03a92a1e7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/57210a09be5bbd38e4334ec4feda5e03a92a1e7a"}],"sha":"7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/7f500645d158e928ee5c8bf23b73147d47c25e37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/57210a09be5bbd38e4334ec4feda5e03a92a1e7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T22:24:39Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T22:24:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(just): make lint-llm-diff''s first argument a diff base, not a file (#65)\n\n## What\nPublish the change on this branch. It is finished, tested, and needs no\nrework.\n\nThe branch carries `1ee4dda fix(just): make lint-llm-diff''s first\nargument a diff base,\nnot a file`, plus two harness provenance commits on top — an empty\n`chore: orchestrated change (incomplete step)` marker and a\n`chore: attest verified recovery of preserved work`.\n\nYour whole job is: run the repository''s gate, and let the lifecycle\npublish the branch.\n\n- **Do not** modify the change, its message, or the two provenance\ncommits.\n- **Do not** run `just lint-llm-diff` against the real judge to\ndemonstrate the fix. Its\nbehavior is already proven by\n`apps/shell-e2e/src/unit/lint-llm-diff.spec.ts`, which\ndrives the real recipe with a recording stub and asserts the argv it\nhands over. That\ntest runs inside the gate. A live judged run would spend a model call\nper case and make\na deterministic check depend on the network, which is exactly what that\ntest''s\n  `ignore-block[e2e_not_mocked]` justification rejects.\n- **Do not** widen scope. If you believe something is wrong with the\nchange, stop and say\n  so in your report instead of fixing it.\n\nIf the gate passes, you are done — report it and let publication\nproceed.\n\n## Why\nThis change has been finished for hours and has failed to land four\ntimes, never once\nbecause the change was wrong: one dispatch never ran the gate, one had a\ncommit subject\ntwo characters too long, one ran in a worktree with no workspace install\nso the pre-push\nguard died silently, and one burned its turn cap re-proving what a\ncommitted test already\nproves. Meanwhile `just lint-llm-diff` remains the pre-push enforcement\npoint in a\nrepository with no CI, and passing it a ref still silently narrows the\nrun to the subset\nof rules whose own `files` globs survive — a confident pass over a\nfraction of the\nruleset. A false green there is the difference between a gate and the\nappearance of one.\n\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\n08c1c4f2f1f0b5e9bc89ddb97a6041829024a253\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d30bd7ce2326a8575e8036bddedf9b5401b058b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/d30bd7ce2326a8575e8036bddedf9b5401b058b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/57210a09be5bbd38e4334ec4feda5e03a92a1e7a","verification":{"payload":"tree d30bd7ce2326a8575e8036bddedf9b5401b058b5\nparent 3db2b3785daa5de07a8bd961616fcd3053380937\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785709479 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785709479 +0000\n\nfix(just): make lint-llm-diff''s first argument a diff base, not a file (#65)\n\n## What\nPublish the change on this branch. It is finished, tested, and needs no\nrework.\n\nThe branch carries `1ee4dda fix(just): make lint-llm-diff''s first\nargument a diff base,\nnot a file`, plus two harness provenance commits on top — an empty\n`chore: orchestrated change (incomplete step)` marker and a\n`chore: attest verified recovery of preserved work`.\n\nYour whole job is: run the repository''s gate, and let the lifecycle\npublish the branch.\n\n- **Do not** modify the change, its message, or the two provenance\ncommits.\n- **Do not** run `just lint-llm-diff` against the real judge to\ndemonstrate the fix. Its\nbehavior is already proven by\n`apps/shell-e2e/src/unit/lint-llm-diff.spec.ts`, which\ndrives the real recipe with a recording stub and asserts the argv it\nhands over. That\ntest runs inside the gate. A live judged run would spend a model call\nper case and make\na deterministic check depend on the network, which is exactly what that\ntest''s\n  `ignore-block[e2e_not_mocked]` justification rejects.\n- **Do not** widen scope. If you believe something is wrong with the\nchange, stop and say\n  so in your report instead of fixing it.\n\nIf the gate passes, you are done — report it and let publication\nproceed.\n\n## Why\nThis change has been finished for hours and has failed to land four\ntimes, never once\nbecause the change was wrong: one dispatch never ran the gate, one had a\ncommit subject\ntwo characters too long, one ran in a worktree with no workspace install\nso the pre-push\nguard died silently, and one burned its turn cap re-proving what a\ncommitted test already\nproves. Meanwhile `just lint-llm-diff` remains the pre-push enforcement\npoint in a\nrepository with no CI, and passing it a ref still silently narrows the\nrun to the subset\nof rules whose own `files` globs survive — a confident pass over a\nfraction of the\nruleset. A false green there is the difference between a gate and the\nappearance of one.\n\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\n08c1c4f2f1f0b5e9bc89ddb97a6041829024a253\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb8OnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANtsQAEny+XAGDQrtW0cE0/BydlqI\nAVIGv8zERd0AUsJoHJQWdHclpfGppcISHYCS7T6jfBYC9UeHBp2aGeEkQ5gsqCFW\nfmCUDlS/L55pZS5qs2jnulL8LhwofolHq71qbP+b7bOexbPzXZqMrn8HZH7rCO7N\ndSD2djLjNPlvWnoRYy/+3DvRmU4UmjxTdBQR0AWI8tXgcn8oAL1TsXiz9Xl7gGip\nhoYdO6OVLI136hIEU5a6Puq/NHl79SPgCUXT1t2vUtRJJda7DSr03bj4mQK2+gcZ\nM4FXaRIBXzLeyzyMJqRICGeDPdwICjttvUXK1fyh8xE6KS26rphr+XPYUy+D/JgG\nS6upePi6rzyF+FSSF77a+8WmjwfuD+BO2+KnJSogf/mLO/T6N6Fv48rRwJNsShPS\nuI1h6mHNdJNCqCaJPV0Nh4d9b1fKel8Y4CfFh5Nna0DcspMNQegOt3MdXtN7UH+N\nqJIgVJw0ht232Lh9H5blZpJa0STY5q3KlCF7enhavhty5WCREF/OvYOBWaXeHg5t\nAjxNiXn0b/XQpKAN3Ywwk3sHjvobQzKp/C7wgEVbpkQU9rgC0k38C+OZ3fIaK1hx\nUREngN28FiVnZPI/Y+UpWmQEPtorqwtcQ79G+4CVvO9HulhcWdUvgmbnKUY52w12\n2xHiPToZkKp/nlCdnWku\n=tMFD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T22:24:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https:/