tps://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/3db2b3785daa5de07a8bd961616fcd3053380937/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T16:40:00Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T16:40:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(courses): explain the preview loading timer (#64)\n\n## What\nNote that `loading` is a preview scenario rather than a real fetch\nstate, and that the 1.5s timer exists so a previewed skeleton resolves\ninstead of sticking.\n\n## Why\nCourses arrive synchronously from the data client, so an unexplained\ntimer that flips view state reads like a race workaround. Saying what it\nis prevents someone removing it as dead code or copying it into a pane\nthat does fetch.\n\nScoped to `apps/courses/` alone. Paired with the `apps/bio/` change so\nthe two publish lanes overlap, exercising the compose-and-deploy `queue:\nmax` / `cancel-in-progress: false` concurrency landed in #60.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"658259d8ac0df252a3ff04b44f1268cf29827d1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/658259d8ac0df252a3ff04b44f1268cf29827d1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/3db2b3785daa5de07a8bd961616fcd3053380937","verification":{"payload":"tree 658259d8ac0df252a3ff04b44f1268cf29827d1d\nparent 5a67ab5faef728b3e844e454c599549c38fadeda\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785688800 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785688800 -0600\n\ndocs(courses): explain the preview loading timer (#64)\n\n## What\nNote that `loading` is a preview scenario rather than a real fetch\nstate, and that the 1.5s timer exists so a previewed skeleton resolves\ninstead of sticking.\n\n## Why\nCourses arrive synchronously from the data client, so an unexplained\ntimer that flips view state reads like a race