hub.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/c1de1c938f4807180f45ecf02cee412d7b5215b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T16:05:13Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T16:05:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(awards): name the empty and error state copy (#61)\n\n## What\nDestructure the awards state copy into `heading` and `detail` instead of\nindexing an anonymous array at `copy[0]` / `copy[1]`.\n\n## Why\nPositional indexing hid which string was the heading and which the body\nat the point of use. Naming them makes the two-state union readable\nwithout scrolling back to the literal.\n\nThis change is deliberately scoped to `apps/awards/` alone: it doubles\nas the awards-only probe for the new per-app publish topology landed in\n#60, which must select exactly one publish lane for a single-app change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"be46111d373343c737bc19db3ad0af67a5ffc2b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/be46111d373343c737bc19db3ad0af67a5ffc2b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/c1de1c938f4807180f45ecf02cee412d7b5215b5","verification":{"payload":"tree be46111d373343c737bc19db3ad0af67a5ffc2b0\nparent 55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785686713 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785686713 -0600\n\nrefactor(awards): name the empty and error state copy (#61)\n\n## What\nDestructure the awards state copy into `heading` and `detail` instead of\nindexing an anonymous array at `copy[0]` / `copy[1]`.\n\n## Why\nPositional indexing hid which string was the heading and which the body\nat the point of use. Naming them makes the two-state union readable\nwithout scrolling back to the literal.\n\nThis change is deliberately scoped to `apps/awards/` alone: it doubles\nas the awards-only probe for the new per-app publish topology landed in\n#60, which must select exactly one publish lane for a single-app change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb2q5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAerUQAF43w7YzpnLNMTE4MAl0guu6\nv40KQ6Qipj5KrJBKmsuRjQQvnzK/udCSQ9PGkdMt73SKSOdZXOAMdh67R8Obshic\nemD53Xa4K509WXVgcgVQSpJy+rap4JRjIzLSrIUhs5nr4Pp+XXho8JTTBZL4yFhl\n/jqK2MYEiNoT1SIYBIqoExjtH/JTl1QkYHQU+zd7Nfj3VJ2YsN7enj+F+oAxvlU/\nQ2fkN0zgtdRKbNT+5vWwNQLSY8AaJ1lYrXCp80EX83oe5YAI5y3DJmwFb1seLLj5\nopMQPvOXL/1F/rh5aDG+7ZDlL1WPg8E4C4AFV+85MBx/zoapxb2F7Fcu0aivokUF\nrgHo4nMKHXGQqbmfCMFn3t1S45wUyDbMJIgmNBd/atopZyeRt6nDOTnJXxuMWjtE\ndFcBr9XhhoLxDbtSOqrLrX0SnHwrD0LVd9qOPXYeA5I0Nzvnql+y1byfIN6Iyv2x\nuGhMtlZ7PqXgWlmICHPNfnSmO5hBSQ0i1CKvPyA3zdy4uB62uCKYtz90pzuUbhQO\nsbh8H2ve1wduI/fdVwkhoVlFozSzUvk7AgKomDX1mtYCeNy8k+iwyF/BFJuHu4m6\nGsxHyXhN7jefbK5zsgW52J1HxEooam4t2uFWS5rXv6pPJi3gTIk0TpDfLUsjIU95\n/b+PkvmcmAZ58jOgYfq6\n=vYHV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T16:05:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/c1de1c938f4807180f45ecf02cee412d7b5215b5","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKGMxZGUxYzkzOGY0ODA3MTgwZjQ1ZWNmMDJjZWU0MTJkN2I1MjE1YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100","sha":"55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100"}],"sha":"c1de1c938f4807180f45ecf02cee412d7b5215b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/c1de1c938f4807180f45ecf02cee412d7b5215b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T15:27:19Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T15:27:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): publish each app independently, compose and deploy once; vali… (#60)\n\n## What\nReplace the single monolithic Pages build with independent per-app\npublish lanes plus one serialized compose-and-deploy lane.\n\n`.github/workflows/pages.yml` today runs `nx run shell:prerender` —\nwhich builds every app — and uploads `dist/apps/shell` as the Pages\nartifact. Replace that with:\n\n- An affected job that selects the apps a push to `master` actually\nchanged.\n- One publish lane per selected app, each writing **only its own\nsubtree** (bundle, fragment HTML, fragment CSS, contract JSON) to a\ncontent-store branch.\n- One compose-and-deploy job that checks out the content store, runs the\ncompose script from the previous task over whatever is currently\npublished, and performs `actions/upload-pages-artifact` followed by\n`actions/deploy-pages`.\n\nConstraints that are load-bearing:\n\n- **Keep Pages on `build_type: workflow`.** Do not switch the site to a\nserved branch. The artifact deploy is what avoids GitHub''s legacy Pages\nbuild race — where a newer build kills an in-flight one and records it\n`errored` with duration 0 — and it is also why the 10-builds-per-hour\nsoft limit does not apply here. The content-store branch is storage only\nand must never become the served source.\n- The compose-and-deploy job carries a concurrency group with `queue:\nmax` and `cancel-in-progress: false`. The default `queue: single`\ncancels the pending run when a third arrives, which would silently drop\nmost lanes'' deploys. Note that `queue: max` combined with\n`cancel-in-progress: true` is a workflow validation error.\n- Compose must be **idempotent full-state**: it always assembles current\npublished state, so a cancelled or superseded compose run loses nothing\nand the next one publishes everything.\n- Publish lanes must not destroy each other''s work on the content-store\nbranch. Each writes only its own subtree and recovers from a\nnon-fast-forward push.\n\nDocument the resulting topology in `docs/architecture.md` and\n`AGENTS.md`, including why the content store is not the served branch.\n\n## Why\nProving the microfrontend architecture means proving independent\ndeployability against a real deploy target, and GitHub Pages is that\ntarget. Under Pages a deployed artifact is always the whole site, so the\nonly way to get independent deployment without a repository per app is\nto separate publishing a unit''s bytes from assembling and deploying the\nsite. Without this the previous task''s decoupling stays theoretical,\nsince every deploy would still rebuild everything.\n\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\nd10cb009099662e41346e6ae0dad6e67207430cb\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\nafef98ed27230650a0436a2c7148eb7f38aad375\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60d1795148f38ca25ddbdec23203c6356e414bcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/60d1795148f38ca25ddbdec23203c6356e414bcf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100","verification":{"payload":"tree 60d1795148f38ca25ddbdec23203c6356e414bcf\nparent 32a6c0861fb7b139ecffa901bd6c4e79213f0165\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785684439 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785684439 +0000\n\nfeat(ci): publish each app independently, compose and deploy once; vali… (#60)\n\n## What\nReplace the single monolithic Pages build with independent per-app\npublish lanes plus one serialized compose-and-deploy lane.\n\n`.github/workflows/pages.yml` today runs `nx run shell:prerender` —\nwhich builds every app — and uploads `dist/apps/shell` as the Pages\nartifact. Replace that with:\n\n- An affected job that selects the apps a push to `master` actually\nchanged.\n- One publish lane per selected app, each writing **only its own\nsubtree** (bundle, fragment HTML, fragment CSS, contract JSON) to a\ncontent-store branch.\n- One compose-and-deploy job that checks out the content store, runs the\ncompose script from the previous task over whatever is currently\npublished, and performs `actions/upload-pages-artifact` followed by\n`actions/deploy-pages`.\n\nConstraints that are load-bearing:\n\n- **Keep Pages on `build_type: workflow`.** Do not switch the site to a\nserved branch. The artifact deploy is what avoids GitHub''s legacy Pages\nbuild race — where a newer build kills an in-flight one and records it\n`errored` with duration 0 — and it is also why the 10-builds-per-hour\nsoft limit does not apply here. The content-store branch is storage only\nand must never become the served source.\n- The compose-and-deploy job carries a concurrency group with `queue:\nmax` and `cancel-in-progress: false`. The default `queue: single`\ncancels the pending run when a third arrives, which would silently drop\nmost lanes'' deploys. Note that `queue: max` combined with\n`cancel-in-progress: true` is a workflow validation error.\n- Compose must be **idempotent full-state**: it always assembles current\npublished state, so a cancelled or superseded compose run loses nothing\nand the next one publishes everything.\n- Publish lanes must not destroy each other''s work on the content-store\nbranch. Each writes only its own subtree and recovers from a\nnon-fast-forward push.\n\nDocument the resulting topology in `docs/architecture.md` and\n`AGENTS.md`, including why the content store is not the served branch.\n\n## Why\nProving the microfrontend architecture means proving independent\ndeployability against a real deploy target, and GitHub Pages is that\ntarget. Under Pages a deployed artifact is always the whole site, so the\nonly way to get independent deployment without a repository per app is\nto separate publishing a unit''s bytes from assembling and deploying the\nsite. Without this the previous task''s decoupling stays theoretical,\nsince every deploy would still rebuild everything.\n\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\nd10cb009099662e41346e6ae0dad6e67207430cb\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\nafef98ed27230650a0436a2c7148eb7f38aad375\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb2HXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAP4QAAS9P10lrzuq9356twYb0z1x\nN0myyYCdDkoxufV0sz1+m+mh8DzZ6pMoTslUQuBT23W6hgkemmhjf2V/gx50IJSU\n94jgsqFJLwdCnb9XxuFrmNf/s/3HLzgCSkmYB8J7R0Af7QSGmTKk6bBaWwcFkPE2\nXZgLpCyj1Z1U7BEZl673l44nGMfo4kzQYFLoX0oNHEwwC7akwmWV12nYrMCEeUum\nKpxzgKZG9pulFamMfVLZt1lx8NzADE6L78kZQbp0V/2P+skeUnSQcop09cUzLdxz\nFuZLLDTpptyOiDp3LHkb2+Wlp1D5Q39FVHfKtV3LJimk0drhVO3jKQ9SLXOYC1WN\nfeRsk30bb8G2O7kGiNA4CxUdYhFXGTP3CDprROj3K9pTequevpZc5RwvAp0SwCjv\ncS7IdjDJygb8E1tT3P5Tnx7KQ2kolBZnTMC5oMblMKsUC/un+0nlU+Tomh4+k9fq\ntayC2Rf/W4gK9jeRezkojFndvhKu2Hs8XOxC2qAQpY0CNLy/8KG2QqYySpzc/odj\nEN6b9IADer+dJ9eHzaPdm2rACnHDEynzxn5FxCkbqvVaLypixNMXP298rZ+pAoq8\nKlGEUI5GyETXKTcv5R/66Kh+TAlqTZsE9rA+lBOv99l7+U2PelEr6jQbJF0c/tTz\n4gni1BBFCvRl6tmW4clC\n=Rq20\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T15:27:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDU1YmMwZWUxNjMyOWVkY2NjZDhmNzdjNTBmZTQ2M2ZjZDM5MDgxMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/32a6c0861fb7b139ecffa901bd6c4e79213f0165","sha":"32a6c0861fb7b139ecffa901bd6c4e79213f0165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/32a6c0861fb7b139ecffa901bd6c4e79213f0165"}],"sha":"55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/55bc0ee16329edcccd8f77c50fe463fcd3908100"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/32a6c0861fb7b139ecffa901bd6c4e79213f0165/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T18:48:04Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T18:48:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: compose pages from published fragments; tolerate unavailable sour… (#59)\n\n## What\nFinish and publish the published-fragment composition work already on\nthis branch, and fix the one defect that blocks its publication.\n\n**The branch already carries the implementation.** Commit `20e8bbb\nfeat(ssg): compose pages from published fragments` sits on top of\npreserved checkpoint `162754f`. It introduces `scripts/compose.mjs` and\nits spec, `libs/build-config/src/published-fragment.ts`,\n`libs/build-config/src/fragment-contract.ts` plus schema and spec,\n`scripts/shell-fragment-entry.tsx`, `scripts/home-fragment-page.tsx`,\ncompose-time gating in `scripts/check-static-artifact.mjs`, and deletes\n`scripts/build-prerender-renderer.mjs` — the module that imported all\ntwelve remotes from `apps/*/src/page` and server-rendered them into the\nshell. That deletion is the point of the whole task.\n\n**The blocking defect.** `libs/build-config/src/published-fragment.ts`\ncalls `git rev-parse HEAD` in `sourceRevision()` (around line 26,\ninvoked from around line 129) to stamp a source revision into each app''s\nfragment contract. That works on the host and fails deterministically\ninside the Playwright screenshot container: the container mounts only\nthe worktree at `/work`, and a git worktree''s `.git` is a pointer file\nto the parent clone''s git directory on the host, which is not mounted.\nThe recorded gate log shows the exact failure:\n\n```\nfatal: not a git repository: .../.clone/.git/worktrees/ai-orchestrator-engineer-73a4ccb2-c9f1f59585\nError: Command failed: git rev-parse HEAD\n    at sourceRevision (/work/libs/build-config/src/published-fragment.ts:26:89)\n```\n\nFix it so the source revision is supplied by an injected value — an\nenvironment variable stamped by the caller — and degrades gracefully\nwhen git is unreachable, either omitting the field or using a documented\nplaceholder. It must never hard-fail a build. Add a test that exercises\nthe no-git path explicitly.\n\n**Verify the path that actually broke.** Screenshot capture is\ndeliberately NOT part of `just check` in this repository; it runs in the\n`.githooks/pre-push` guard. A green `just check && just lint-llm-diff`\ntherefore cannot prove the containerised capture path, which is exactly\nwhy this defect reached publication. You must explicitly exercise the\nvisual capture path for at least one app, and report its command output,\nbefore claiming done.\n\n**The type-check OOM is very likely fallout, not a second bug.** The\nsame gate log shows `RpcExitError: Process 276 exited [SIGTERM]` and\nthen `[type-check] Issues checking service aborted - probably out of\nmemory` — after, and downstream of, the git failure. Confirm that it\ndisappears once the git defect is fixed. Only if it persists should you\ntreat it as an independent memory ceiling, and then report it rather\nthan tuning limits blindly.\n\n## Why\nThe site''s twelve microfrontends are independently built and\nindependently tested but cannot be independently deployed:\n`shell:prerender` depends on a source build of every remote, so changing\none app rebuilds and redeploys all thirteen units. This branch already\nbreaks that coupling and proved it — the worker''s own report recorded\nthat an `awards`-only change now selects `build awards` only, with no\nprerender. That proof is worth nothing until the work can actually\npublish, and one unsatisfiable build-time git call is the only thing\nstanding between the two.\n\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\n162754f218ee8427da9caa990de99ef18e4b2152\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc311aae1536f0da0167e9c1c10f5decd021ba57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/fc311aae1536f0da0167e9c1c10f5decd021ba57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/32a6c0861fb7b139ecffa901bd6c4e79213f0165","verification":{"payload":"tree fc311aae1536f0da0167e9c1c10f5decd021ba57\nparent 3418e8cd4234d499afdf058175fbd96fed0b4145\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785610084 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785610084 +0000\n\nfeat: compose pages from published fragments; tolerate unavailable sour… (#59)\n\n## What\nFinish and publish the published-fragment composition work already on\nthis branch, and fix the one defect that blocks its publication.\n\n**The branch already carries the implementation.** Commit `20e8bbb\nfeat(ssg): compose pages from published fragments` sits on top of\npreserved checkpoint `162754f`. It introduces `scripts/compose.mjs` and\nits spec, `libs/build-config/src/published-fragment.ts`,\n`libs/build-config/src/fragment-contract.ts` plus schema and spec,\n`scripts/shell-fragment-entry.tsx`, `scripts/home-fragment-page.tsx`,\ncompose-time gating in `scripts/check-static-artifact.mjs`, and deletes\n`scripts/build-prerender-renderer.mjs` — the module that imported all\ntwelve remotes from `apps/*/src/page` and server-rendered them into the\nshell. That deletion is the point of the whole task.\n\n**The blocking defect.** `libs/build-config/src/published-fragment.ts`\ncalls `git rev-parse HEAD` in `sourceRevision()` (around line 26,\ninvoked from around line 129) to stamp a source revision into each app''s\nfragment contract. That works on the host and fails deterministically\ninside the Playwright screenshot container: the container mounts only\nthe worktree at `/work`, and a git worktree''s `.git` is a pointer file\nto the parent clone''s git directory on the host, which is not mounted.\nThe recorded gate log shows the exact failure:\n\n```\nfatal: not a git repository: .../.clone/.git/worktrees/ai-orchestrator-engineer-73a4ccb2-c9f1f59585\nError: Command failed: git rev-parse HEAD\n    at sourceRevision (/work/libs/build-config/src/published-fragment.ts:26:89)\n```\n\nFix it so the source revision is supplied by an injected value — an\nenvironment variable stamped by the caller — and degrades gracefully\nwhen git is unreachable, either omitting the field or using a documented\nplaceholder. It must never hard-fail a build. Add a test that exercises\nthe no-git path explicitly.\n\n**Verify the path that actually broke.** Screenshot capture is\ndeliberately NOT part of `just check` in this repository; it runs in the\n`.githooks/pre-push` guard. A green `just check && just lint-llm-diff`\ntherefore cannot prove the containerised capture path, which is exactly\nwhy this defect reached publication. You must explicitly exercise the\nvisual capture path for at least one app, and report its command output,\nbefore claiming done.\n\n**The type-check OOM is very likely fallout, not a second bug.** The\nsame gate log shows `RpcExitError: Process 276 exited [SIGTERM]` and\nthen `[type-check] Issues checking service aborted - probably out of\nmemory` — after, and downstream of, the git failure. Confirm that it\ndisappears once the git defect is fixed. Only if it persists should you\ntreat it as an independent memory ceiling, and then report it rather\nthan tuning limits blindly.\n\n## Why\nThe site''s twelve microfrontends are independently built and\nindependently tested but cannot be independently deployed:\n`shell:prerender` depends on a source build of every remote, so changing\none app rebuilds and redeploys all thirteen units. This branch already\nbreaks that coupling and proved it — the worker''s own report recorded\nthat an `awards`-only change now selects `build awards` only, with no\nprerender. That proof is worth nothing until the work can actually\npublish, and one unsatisfiable build-time git call is the only thing\nstanding between the two.\n\nOrchestrator-Recovered-Incomplete:\n162754f218ee8427da9caa990de99ef18e4b2152\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbj9kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAumMQAANbaHVk7+b7L5x80gppfrl+\nnfjLO60mKGRFyuE6mYibmt0koZF1fvqraO1dyRv1LI3wSpZwRzAzuD7H0FBKgUnQ\n92s6s5Y0ZV4ZKNBARpHEIue0QvQtC5DePyWQ7IrM/zS6vjDqt91VG2ZgvE3bNmtK\nvFKqzzZjOObsT8680U8NPsOt52o7PCxVm0UvLNqTC2D9rskD2ZBRVGz7SWx4Mp8k\nQlT3o8+1RABWqGe05cKcLyjHk8nfBKJ9b5VDNanKJTmS4mlvNFOK2mcAKKJYvmoO\ne2dNqFzzZqmZoMSsa9dh7I1DuZR8H+4HgsamuFM6+Ys1RpElCXkxug2ze0es17Yb\nCH/zvHkJ+DLRFzti27frZ0Pg+n3i/I6etAZjHsf7EQeHPYNewrK3pA+9Tfy2Ywqm\njroyAFxU5Hw0DWFPkhqPEbqoG+2dmIrlGK2Kq1nGd8SD09Xe+L6Rjbw8y0pEg0nr\nXBszetfS615Xia1KCSsRBeVtvGcL/P8yAJ9SToxW92qopna+Y20zr4w/3kxs1DNq\nCYmsG2BoB9KxWs74c6c5Dkk7speWor9hYWB14uRPdKrdScZHbHuQXDz6VOfpOvQy\nRry6aagvPTGtufS/RirTyR+kKWTHzXyn0NOuohnLg5KZ+JVoeRm+bUXPLpVrL9Na\nGIk8sM6W6Pr6rk5PHdiv\n=VfuJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:48:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"htt