rcontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/6e30f8b82d4a0dc90f8ef363b2675696c47a91bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T04:47:04Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T04:47:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: hydrate only the active route''s remote and lazy-load the rest (#55)\n\n## What\nStop gating startup on the whole federation graph.\n`apps/shell/src/main.tsx` currently awaits all five route remotes before\ncreating the router and hydrating (lines 10-16). Change it to determine\nthe active route (the `data-prerendered-route` attribute on `#root` —\nalready read by the home remote — with a pathname fallback), await only\nthat remote''s `Page` for hydration, and register the other routes with\nlazy components (`lazyRouteComponent(() => import(\"<remote>/Page\"))`\nfrom `@tanstack/react-router` 1.170.18) so their `remoteEntry.js` and\nchunks load on demand and are preloaded by hover intent together with\ntheir loaders.\n\nPreserve the intent-preload behavior that landed just before this: the\nhome route''s loader must first await `import(\"home/Page\")` and then call\nits `preload()`. Preserve hydration correctness and the pre-hydration\nbehavior where server-rendered anchors perform plain static navigations.\n\n## Why\nToday roughly 1MB of compressed JavaScript (540KB shell main plus twelve\n~37KB remoteEntries plus chunks) must arrive before anything is\ninteractive, which delays hydration, keeps early clicks falling back to\nfull static loads, and wastes bandwidth on four routes the visitor may\nnever open. The owner wants the static page to hydrate into a SPA\npromptly, with the *hover* — not startup — being what fetches the next\npage.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79515059dec230b9bf6eab19f9e7bbedd48e0991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/79515059dec230b9bf6eab19f9e7bbedd48e0991"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/6e30f8b82d4a0dc90f8ef363b2675696c47a91bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 79515059dec230b9bf6eab19f9e7bbedd48e0991\nparent 352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785214024 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785214024 +0000\n\nfeat: hydrate only the active route''s remote and lazy-load the rest (#55)\n\n## What\nStop gating startup on the whole federation graph.\n`apps/shell/src/main.tsx` currently awaits all five route remotes before\ncreating the router and hydrating (lines 10-16). Change it to determine\nthe active route (the `data-prerendered-route` attribute on `#root` —\nalready read by the home remote — with a pathname fallback), await only\nthat remote''s `Page` for hydration, and register the other routes with\nlazy components (`lazyRouteComponent(() => import(\"<remote>/Page\"))`\nfrom `@tanstack/react-router` 1.170.18) so their `remoteEntry.js` and\nchunks load on demand and are preloaded by hover intent together with\ntheir loaders.\n\nPreserve the intent-preload behavior that landed just before this: the\nhome route''s loader must first await `import(\"home/Page\")` and then call\nits `preload()`. Preserve hydration correctness and the pre-hydration\nbehavior where server-rendered anchors perform plain static navigations.\n\n## Why\nToday roughly 1MB of compressed JavaScript (540KB shell main plus twelve\n~37KB remoteEntries plus chunks) must arrive before anything is\ninteractive, which delays hydration, keeps early clicks falling back to\nfull static loads, and wastes bandwidth on four routes the visitor may\nnever open. The owner wants the static page to hydrate into a SPA\npromptly, with the *hover* — not startup — being what fetches the next\npage.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaDRICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU3EQADZScYcJK/bRPC+dHxXtCrHr\n8N30LaOwM7cvb141G0sxF7GypQks2Kpn4cx+XYdp4AU5itxIrCGWJmlSTpoWbLjV\nqFe8AeqBM/RSxJhhsmTVp89JL7uQYHp/ZrummjVjwJZq3ltp3esmlaQ3NlI7Z4Hg\nOyFJ8IrBEo9pIsjnxnhp/SCf5Z25oSTpGpPUmK3JtRUaJV0FMgxnuj/tAOrOv9F/\nIWxRrB13UdJN272qaJfNQLoFmLQ8nFr/vMRg6ZoJUFJ+omsQNNMF6uNiu0hsNvyZ\nL4X77NlMp1vUbxD7RJNiCKj6tu4aYXKnWgQ9VTDMc1vb1gerMtkOWiypra2A19wS\nrAB5FGyg/4YoyYQzp+aTncKVj+pi7EbztiJ3OZ7i1f6ekuav2rKUzDdRMCpPRIXn\n6lZn5QUOP7XhaLzvgFJcK0i7i7pY4IYX3adak5rdqC8jjiHrkdtQMxOy++bUFT1L\nILJlL26Id0JZyxm1uCZsWUh1YMwaTTSX6YLslb1Qg6Gd4pjUt/Pj7aAvSFOI7Rd2\n0p4QvD+n2fAVRXUPbSD4ZtyhTC2byuxyp1E3lyDW3d+uBo+f1cG6oDvDWUfu8/90\nkxCr7dyrmVvQX26V3ZxQ3YRzIHujPbzAIpOe3tEnlTAraaVjvvq1HQKmCMF0kiNi\ni7agfGrSnnsJDMpi/qPv\n=OCVa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T04:47:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/6e30f8b82d4a0dc90f8ef363b2675696c47a91bb","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDZlMzBmOGI4MmQ0YTBkYzkwZjhlZjM2M2IyNjc1Njk2YzQ3YTkxYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b","sha":"352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b"}],"sha":"6e30f8b82d4a0dc90f8ef363b2675696c47a91bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/6e30f8b82d4a0dc90f8ef363b2675696c47a91bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:56:35Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:56:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): make the screencomp capture callback POSIX-correct (#54)\n\n## What\nGet the already-written hover-intent preload change on this branch to a\nfully green required-check set on GitHub so its open PR can merge.\nResume the existing branch\n`ai-orchestrator/engineer/48a7274c-aab0adf129`, which carries PR\nhttps://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/pull/53 (\"feat:\nmake hover intent fully preload home panes and software images\"). The\nfeature work on this branch is already complete and was verified green\nlocally with `just check-all` and `just lint-llm-diff` — do not redo or\nredesign it. Your job is the blocked CI.\n\nThe blocking defect is in this repository''s own\n`.github/workflows/visual-docs.yml`. Its `capture-command:` input\n(around lines 104-111) is injected as the container callback of the\nreusable workflow\n`nickderobertis/screencomp/.github/workflows/visual-docs-reusable.yml@v0.4.5`,\nand that callback is executed by `sh` (dash), not bash. Line 107 uses\nthe bash-only construct:\n\n```\n[[ \"$SCREENCOMP_PROJECT\" =~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$ ]] || {\n  echo \"capture-command: SCREENCOMP_PROJECT must be a valid Nx project name\" >&2\n```\n\nso every capture leg dies immediately with:\n\n```\n/__w/_temp/<uuid>.sh: 3: [[: not found\ncapture-command: SCREENCOMP_PROJECT must be a valid Nx project name\n##[error]Process completed with exit code 2.\n```\n\nOn PR #53 this fails `visual-docs / capture (x86_64, home, ...)` and\n`visual-docs / capture (x86_64, awards, ...)`; `visual-docs / report`\nand `visual-docs / aggregate-comment` then skip, and `classify-gate`\nfails reporting \"screencomp reported visual drift or failed (failure);\nreview the per-app gallery and PR comment, regenerate the baseline\nlocally with the pre-push guard, and commit it\". That message\nmisattributes a shell-portability bug as a visual regression. `check`,\n`affected`, `llmlint`, `visual-docs / pages-preflight`, and `visual-docs\n/ arches` are all already SUCCESS on this PR.\n\nDo the following:\n\n1. Confirm the actual interpreter and failure rather than assuming this\ndiagnosis — read the screencomp v0.4.5 reusable workflow to see how\n`capture-command` is injected and executed, and confirm from the failing\njob logs.\n2. Make the callback correct under the shell that actually runs it,\nkeeping the same validation intent (reject a `SCREENCOMP_PROJECT` that\nis not a plausible Nx project name) and the same error message and exit\nstatus. Prefer fixing the callback in this repository over pinning or\nforking screencomp; if the correct fix genuinely belongs upstream or in\nthe reusable workflow''s inputs, say so explicitly and explain why.\n3. Once capture actually runs, determine whether there is *genuine*\nvisual drift for `home` and `awards`. This branch deliberately makes a\npreloaded Home mount without skeletons and shares one awards request\nbetween the warm and the mount, so a legitimate baseline change is\nplausible. If the baselines genuinely need regenerating, regenerate them\nthrough this repository''s documented baseline flow (the pre-push guard\nreferenced by `classify-gate`) and commit them. If there is no drift,\nstate that plainly rather than refreshing baselines to force green.\n4. Add coverage that would have caught this locally: a non-POSIX\nconstruct in an injected screencomp callback must fail a local check\nrather than only surfacing as a red CI leg. The repository already has a\nvisual-contract verifier and `lint-workflows` (actionlint + shellcheck)\n— extend whichever is the right home for this, in this repository''s own\ntesting style.\n5. Watch the PR''s checks to completion with `gh` and confirm every\nrequired check passes. Do not merge by hand and do not disable, skip, or\nmake non-required any check to get green.\n\n## Why\nThe owner wants the loading rework live on the deployed site. The\nhover-intent preload work is finished and locally proven but has been\nstranded in an unmergeable PR, and every downstream piece of the loading\nrework depends on it landing. The failure is also actively misleading:\n`classify-gate` tells a reader to regenerate visual baselines when the\nreal cause is a bash-only test running under dash, so the next person to\nhit it would be sent to refresh baselines that were never wrong. Fixing\nthe callback unblocks this PR and stops that misdiagnosis from recurring\non every future PR whose affected set includes a capture leg.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1603309dbac3ee80d1c78e6d1b829786817482a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/1603309dbac3ee80d1c78e6d1b829786817482a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1603309dbac3ee80d1c78e6d1b829786817482a6\nparent 0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785153395 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785153395 +0000\n\nfix(ci): make the screencomp capture callback POSIX-correct (#54)\n\n## What\nGet the already-written hover-intent preload change on this branch to a\nfully green required-check set on GitHub so its open PR can merge.\nResume the existing branch\n`ai-orchestrator/engineer/48a7274c-aab0adf129`, which carries PR\nhttps://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/pull/53 (\"feat:\nmake hover intent fully preload home panes and software images\"). The\nfeature work on this branch is already complete and was verified green\nlocally with `just check-all` and `just lint-llm-diff` — do not redo or\nredesign it. Your job is the blocked CI.\n\nThe blocking defect is in this repository''s own\n`.github/workflows/visual-docs.yml`. Its `capture-command:` input\n(around lines 104-111) is injected as the container callback of the\nreusable workflow\n`nickderobertis/screencomp/.github/workflows/visual-docs-reusable.yml@v0.4.5`,\nand that callback is executed by `sh` (dash), not bash. Line 107 uses\nthe bash-only construct:\n\n```\n[[ \"$SCREENCOMP_PROJECT\" =~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$ ]] || {\n  echo \"capture-command: SCREENCOMP_PROJECT must be a valid Nx project name\" >&2\n```\n\nso every capture leg dies immediately with:\n\n```\n/__w/_temp/<uuid>.sh: 3: [[: not found\ncapture-command: SCREENCOMP_PROJECT must be a valid Nx project name\n##[error]Process completed with exit code 2.\n```\n\nOn PR #53 this fails `visual-docs / capture (x86_64, home, ...)` and\n`visual-docs / capture (x86_64, awards, ...)`; `visual-docs / report`\nand `visual-docs / aggregate-comment` then skip, and `classify-gate`\nfails reporting \"screencomp reported visual drift or failed (failure);\nreview the per-app gallery and PR comment, regenerate the baseline\nlocally with the pre-push guard, and commit it\". That message\nmisattributes a shell-portability bug as a visual regression. `check`,\n`affected`, `llmlint`, `visual-docs / pages-preflight`, and `visual-docs\n/ arches` are all already SUCCESS on this PR.\n\nDo the following:\n\n1. Confirm the actual interpreter and failure rather than assuming this\ndiagnosis — read the screencomp v0.4.5 reusable workflow to see how\n`capture-command` is injected and executed, and confirm from the failing\njob logs.\n2. Make the callback correct under the shell that actually runs it,\nkeeping the same validation intent (reject a `SCREENCOMP_PROJECT` that\nis not a plausible Nx project name) and the same error message and exit\nstatus. Prefer fixing the callback in this repository over pinning or\nforking screencomp; if the correct fix genuinely belongs upstream or in\nthe reusable workflow''s inputs, say so explicitly and explain why.\n3. Once capture actually runs, determine whether there is *genuine*\nvisual drift for `home` and `awards`. This branch deliberately makes a\npreloaded Home mount without skeletons and shares one awards request\nbetween the warm and the mount, so a legitimate baseline change is\nplausible. If the baselines genuinely need regenerating, regenerate them\nthrough this repository''s documented baseline flow (the pre-push guard\nreferenced by `classify-gate`) and commit them. If there is no drift,\nstate that plainly rather than refreshing baselines to force green.\n4. Add coverage that would have caught this locally: a non-POSIX\nconstruct in an injected screencomp callback must fail a local check\nrather than only surfacing as a red CI leg. The repository already has a\nvisual-contract verifier and `lint-workflows` (actionlint + shellcheck)\n— extend whichever is the right home for this, in this repository''s own\ntesting style.\n5. Watch the PR''s checks to completion with `gh` and confirm every\nrequired check passes. Do not merge by hand and do not disable, skip, or\nmake non-required any check to get green.\n\n## Why\nThe owner wants the loading rework live on the deployed site. The\nhover-intent preload work is finished and locally proven but has been\nstranded in an unmergeable PR, and every downstream piece of the loading\nrework depends on it landing. The failure is also actively misleading:\n`classify-gate` tells a reader to regenerate visual baselines when the\nreal cause is a bash-only test running under dash, so the next person to\nhit it would be sent to refresh baselines that were never wrong. Fixing\nthe callback unblocks this PR and stops that misdiagnosis from recurring\non every future PR whose affected set includes a capture leg.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ0dzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQBoQAKkumjJiVpcoXJrGf2TDHW1A\nms03pLFtFOvDT7G2hNVE0pGh7zBNtpG8O/YCEfcq0z8BiIcrbk5UQVSIq1ciAvMn\nMuYoWF7/YzlbelamNk+kOaMkq94rXtWAl+1xWhbzzzySpUPG53A6CH7RxLoToAcm\nuNfTyl8SJUcPPTwlFeZG3tBr1Qt2ssuCaWj53zuKmoImQtRmzK+VnySinmUH43Op\nG1Es/2PwiIGU3sOD2CfH578ro06BiWOTyYK0HyNDO/6SUqm/ClTQz3+RuR6VVPmU\njU1fmqLA8Zl/5K8rQ9/+/XGG40hEhdRpfxBMp1z1jcWyXiQd+aYCxKro3MXGEbTK\nZtWToejKuishhY5cksUe9qiWd+IPG1FacjEcR+JDnbPJDCVkIG0SBNXA4b00/LXi\n7Ry7wuCC0DqN1eAERrnHjvXjs6m9+XZCxbBR8kQVK8xC/ahWcQIhtr1EoQ0jko20\nmEsGFcukVWWpzP7zos0GKbiqvCe/h44z5OCP05LjRuaZNsr6Fe9LOBF148PZ+66k\nTdwUkhe+8rfU2sxxNMMslOnJ6G7XCvIr5Dg6hdcAN72zaLZmzuuwlanLz/b+G0R8\nq2j81M2jf6pwPSeidXLa5qfBsuAifHKOEw21DIobsoGKqxoCISziQ/eYm+QK992b\nI/0GAGnlBMtXkerWmYio\n=Cd4q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T11:56:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDM1MmVlN2YwNTEyMWI1YjZkNzczMTY5YTg3ZWUzNTkzNTljNjdmNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966","sha":"0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966"}],"sha":"352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/352ee7f05121b5b6d773169a87ee359359c67f4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:21:30Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:21:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: make hover intent fully preload home panes and software images (#53)\n\n## What\nMake hover intent actually preload everything a page needs, and make a\npreloaded page mount instantly:\n\n1. Home panes: export a `preload()` from `apps/home/src/page.tsx` that\nresolves the seven pane `Page` modules (their `import()` promises\nalready start at module scope, lines ~27-33) and caches the resolved\ncomponents. Render cached components directly — not through\n`lazy()`/`Suspense` — once resolved, generalizing the existing\nentry-at-`/` `hydratedPanes` mechanism (lines 49-69) to client-side\nnavigation. Add a home-route `loader` in `apps/shell/src/router.tsx`\nthat invokes it; the shell already holds the `home/Page` module\nnamespace in `apps/shell/src/main.tsx`, so the export needs no new\nfederation expose — extend the `RoutePages` wiring to carry it. The\nSSR/prerender path (`scripts/render-entry.tsx` passes plain components)\nmust be unaffected: the loader must no-op or resolve instantly\nserver-side.\n2. Software images: extend the software route loader so that after the\ndomain JSON resolves it warms the unique external `logo_url` images\n(`new Image()`, browser only) so a hover-then-click shows every\ninitially visible card logo with no post-click network fetch.\n3. Fast-click path preserved: a click before preload completes still\nshows the pane/page skeletons and settles correctly.\n\n## Why\nThe intended UX is: hover a link for a moment, then click, and the\nswitch is instant. Today hovering Home issues no requests at all (the\nroute has no loader) and clicking always flashes skeletons — partly\nbecause React `lazy()` suspends on first mount even when its promise\nalready resolved — and hovering Software preloads only the JSON while\nthe logos always load after the click. The owner explicitly wants the\nfull page — code, data, and images — behind a hovered link.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1603309dbac3ee80d1c78e6d1b829786817482a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/1603309dbac3ee80d1c78e6d1b829786817482a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966","verification":{"payload":"tree 1603309dbac3ee80d1c78e6d1b829786817482a6\nparent 190196d839031e3f63f7f8caf2f44f10a0016c21\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785151290 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785151290 +0000\n\nfeat: make hover intent fully preload home panes and software images (#53)\n\n## What\nMake hover intent actually preload everything a page needs, and make a\npreloaded page mount instantly:\n\n1. Home panes: export a `preload()` from `apps/home/src/page.tsx` that\nresolves the seven pane `Page` modules (their `import()` promises\nalready start at module scope, lines ~27-33) and caches the resolved\ncomponents. Render cached components directly — not through\n`lazy()`/`Suspense` — once resolved, generalizing the existing\nentry-at-`/` `hydratedPanes` mechanism (lines 49-69) to client-side\nnavigation. Add a home-route `loader` in `apps/shell/src/router.tsx`\nthat invokes it; the shell already holds the `home/Page` module\nnamespace in `apps/shell/src/main.tsx`, so the export needs no new\nfederation expose — extend the `RoutePages` wiring to carry it. The\nSSR/prerender path (`scripts/render-entry.tsx` passes plain components)\nmust be unaffected: the loader must no-op or resolve instantly\nserver-side.\n2. Software images: extend the software route loader so that after the\ndomain JSON resolves it warms the unique external `logo_url` images\n(`new Image()`, browser only) so a hover-then-click shows every\ninitially visible card logo with no post-click network fetch.\n3. Fast-click path preserved: a click before preload completes still\nshows the pane/page skeletons and settles correctly.\n\n## Why\nThe intended UX is: hover a link for a moment, then click, and the\nswitch is instant. Today hovering Home issues no requests at all (the\nroute has no loader) and clicking always flashes skeletons — partly\nbecause React `lazy()` suspends on first mount even when its promise\nalready resolved — and hovering Software preloads only the JSON while\nthe logos always load after the click. The owner explicitly wants the\nfull page — code, data, and images — behind a hovered link.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZz86CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR/YQAIpQSJMTRj2YG+AObfaIw8vw\n6MCHnpaj73QB583sjOxHaFym7kX1lrXKw49tsRwkl37uDAWaEGJ4dK8HbnRaIzQQ\nCFlIbSWEhn2UjaDKU96KmgcL5IqMNm0TxuQqr9HE6J7KUbWXEaumBKD8DwwJgg8E\n9WRUH8qpo86LbGJO2El8QC+nnw+zQC4CAr34Sn0QoM47tB6JLZC30WMk1O2pHBfo\nR1VT4f80rjykE3cM9Tc1/2T1xuHe3LbS76pk0uftgpfDocjpeMYvM1PVN4bq2yzT\nJ+u4iEE9OuW1xjjPHVvbhcOrMCOzilg2vcazzV3KC6IRzH5b8+w1M+l0K0AQBKUB\nPLaO8X57/TdPj2PAvK+g0kH6P/tcnS/P2VQ57Jg9nw07S/0dE7uTib4wUTUYWhn0\nWuBq2wBufVwnTHUDjRTVRlvykZXSfXxU6FJpBrdrq/WsX7ij3rPdnopA4jE8Dzxe\n/+cjjD+wtaw9aeK7W1SaBqvmrUpQvPLZOc0GGQ5iVpt51pHl288KZDwUjCWGAcny\ntzC2XcnwkvgjEwTw/3+DIsKUXx1pBaBwkBaI3zmzcswHF4qy/5tgyK7zOZslTJHX\niJEzZZIadWH6NerG7exI2UyNWbq2Hm6xFxHW8cfv/6eAQNhwJPSuceOVudLGwKkE\ntJo2PGKJhLgvW1DiXA62\n=+oAf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T11:21:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDA4OTZiNDM0Y2JlZWYyYzUzMjMzOWQxZWI5OTEwMGNiZjNlMDk5NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/190196d839031e3f63f7f8caf2f44f10a0016c21","sha":"190196d839031e3f63f7f8caf2f44f10a0016c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/190196d839031e3f63f7f8caf2f44f10a0016c21"}],"sha":"0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/0896b434cbeef2c532339d1eb99100cbf3e09966"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/190196d839031e3f63f7f8caf2f44f10a0016c21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T03:52:40Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T03:52:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: inline per-route remote CSS into prerendered HTML (#52)\n\n## What\nExtend the prerender pipeline (`scripts/prerender.mjs`) so every\nprerendered route document ships the page-content CSS of every remote\nwhose markup it prerenders, inline in `<head>`, so the static HTML\npaints fully styled before any federation JavaScript arrives.\n\nRoute-to-remote CSS map:\n- `/` -> home, home-carousel, home-cards, home-story, home-contact,\ntimeline, skills, awards\n- `/bio` -> bio; `/research` -> research; `/software` -> software;\n`/courses` -> courses\n\nSource each remote''s hashed `main.*.css` deterministically from its own\nbuilt `index.html` `<link>` tag (the remote builds live under\n`REMOTE_BUILD_ROOT`, default `dist/apps/<name>`; note the route\ndocuments are currently written before remotes are staged into the\nartifact, so read the CSS from the build root or reorder). Dedupe\nidentical CSS payloads before inlining — several remotes re-bundle the\nshared design-system theme. Extend `scripts/check-static-artifact.mjs`\nto fail when a route document lacks its remotes'' inlined CSS, and add a\nJavaScript-disabled shell-e2e assertion proving the styling actually\napplies at first paint.\n\n## Why\nToday the deployed shell links exactly one 767-byte stylesheet covering\nonly the header/nav; every page-body and skeleton rule lives in each\nfederated remote''s CSS and arrives only with that remote''s JS (roughly\n1MB compressed). The site therefore paints its full server-rendered\ncontent unstyled and reflows badly when the CSS lands — the owner sees\nugly first paint and heavy layout shift on every direct load, which\ndefeats the purpose of prerendering real content.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1fffb5c97852ec9783cc56f847822056988c1934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/1fffb5c97852ec9783cc56f847822056988c1934"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/190196d839031e3f63f7f8caf2f44f10a0016c21","verification":{"payload":"tree 1fffb5c97852ec9783cc56f847822056988c1934\nparent 81522ec95612424acd11cfcfbf265db7913dc928\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785124360 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785124360 +0000\n\nfeat: inline per-route remote CSS into prerendered HTML (#52)\n\n## What\nExtend the prerender pipeline (`scripts/prerender.mjs`) so every\nprerendered route document ships the page-content CSS of every remote\nwhose markup it prerenders, inline in `<head>`, so the static HTML\npaints fully styled before any federation JavaScript arrives.\n\nRoute-to-remote CSS map:\n- `/` -> home, home-carousel, home-cards, home-story, home-contact,\ntimeline, skills, awards\n- `/bio` -> bio; `/research` -> research; `/software` -> software;\n`/courses` -> courses\n\nSource each remote''s hashed `main.*.css` deterministically from its own\nbuilt `index.html` `<link>` tag (the remote builds live under\n`REMOTE_BUILD_ROOT`, default `dist/apps/<name>`; note the route\ndocuments are currently written before remotes are staged into the\nartifact, so read the CSS from the build root or reorder). Dedupe\nidentical CSS payloads before inlining — several remotes re-bundle the\nshared design-system theme. Extend `scripts/check-static-artifact.mjs`\nto fail when a route document lacks its remotes'' inlined CSS, and add a\nJavaScript-disabled shell-e2e assertion proving the styling actually\napplies at first paint.\n\n## Why\nToday the deployed shell links exactly one 767-byte stylesheet covering\nonly the header/nav; every page-body and skeleton rule lives in each\nfederated remote''s CSS and arrives only with that remote''s JS (roughly\n1MB compressed). The site therefore paints its full server-rendered\ncontent unstyled and reflows badly when the CSS lands — the owner sees\nugly first paint and heavy layout shift on every direct load, which\ndefeats the purpose of prerendering real content.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick DeRobertis <derobertis.nick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZtYICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz+sQAE+r9mSo6OFRacEwZUKLegkS\nYEnB1NYA0lixAt/73ICjjhu7pcNOwjnte5mxh+V7KXkMFzTQSeXlUKyKc07UwoXw\nwboMVEE2rgpqfVI7Py9QRAWjQnc/gwd9q72ulxTGF2W+OZKu/CwhTP2ipJ3m0Tpj\nhmxchuqwwewBmzJZKSnlDVCTG+rnoeJ5NQenFG2R1/1DxN53kei9qkhAiQIDk8lp\nkSj1chLRWCYVVaZnCszOagiuPAlLyCXwwka5gRINzvvdCEYtXjXwqAdpjNfLj/mH\nPu1ep0dZe/So7CbMOi5a4JOZNufr6M1a7SzQAPY2Ak3WaeEqXB8DmIQ0QOHdGrnt\nsWwqHj6wEHKYuZefGNq+S5M2u8S4dhQTJtSnq4rmWzQz7H66fHQD1414Fyw48ivA\noIoHi6ufRIe4FaFm1d7SKsx3Lqcp8khJJKeoG2W07spThibbsAaIUPxvXyuUgfDH\nqw5a8pXQMrEpNmf8wGABI9QfhvtQ5Kkmq0XhZOMRrXlxf9hFTaJIuDg5TrZCk0jN\n+vLVqE