,"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/81522ec95612424acd11cfcfbf265db7913dc928","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDgxNTIyZWM5NTYxMjQyNGFjZDExY2ZjZmJmMjY1ZGI3OTEzZGM5Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/57c406286d7ba9416b7f44d1fd0f4c105a525638","sha":"57c406286d7ba9416b7f44d1fd0f4c105a525638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/57c406286d7ba9416b7f44d1fd0f4c105a525638"}],"sha":"81522ec95612424acd11cfcfbf265db7913dc928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/81522ec95612424acd11cfcfbf265db7913dc928"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/57c406286d7ba9416b7f44d1fd0f4c105a525638/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T00:10:38Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T00:10:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: validate visual capture project input; host visual docs in dedicat… (#49)\n\n## What\nAdopt the new screencomp release in this repository''s visual-docs\npipeline, so its galleries are hosted in a repository of their own and\nits pull-request comments show real diffs.\n\nFirst determine which screencomp release contains the change. screencomp\nreleases are fully automated: merging to `main` opens a release-plz pull\nrequest that the workflow auto-merges, which tags `vX.Y.Z` and cuts the\nRelease. So the tag may not exist the instant the change merges —\nresolve the newest screencomp release whose commit actually contains the\nexternal-Pages and aggregated-comment work (`gh release list`, `gh\nrelease view`, and the tag''s history), and wait for it rather than\nguessing or pinning a tag that does not exist yet.\n\nThen in `.github/workflows/visual-docs.yml`: advance the\nreusable-workflow ref and `screencomp-version` to that release, and pass\nthe new inputs — `pages-repository:\nnickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site-visual-docs` and the Pages token\nsourced from this repository''s existing `GH_TOKEN` secret (already\nprovisioned with write access to that repository). `comment-mode:\naggregated` and `fail-on-drift: true` stay as they are.\n\nUpdate this repository''s own documentation — `AGENTS.md`, the README,\nand anything under `docs/` that describes the visual-docs loop — to\nstate that galleries now live at\n`https://nickderobertis.github.io/nick-derobertis-site-visual-docs/` and\nwhy: this repository''s own Pages is served from an Actions artifact, so\nits `gh-pages` branch is not served and cannot host them. Leave\n`pages.yml` and the production Pages deploy untouched; that separation\nis the entire reason for the second repository.\n\n## Why\nEvery visual-docs gallery link this repository has ever posted was dead.\nIts Pages site is deployed from an Actions artifact (`build_type:\nworkflow`), so the `gh-pages` branch screencomp deploys galleries to is\nnever served; all twelve links on pull request #47 404''d into the site''s\nown 404 page, which renders the site shell. Pointing screencomp at a\ndedicated Pages repository is what makes visual review work here without\nputting the production site''s deploy at risk.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","tree":{"sha":"38fde7048295a00d70600219d759319fcced10a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/38fde7048295a00d70600219d759319fcced10a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/57c406286d7ba9416b7f44d1fd0f4c105a525638","verification":{"payload":"tree 38fde7048295a00d70600219d759319fcced10a2\nparent 602354205f36418a5729c589eee52d32a2e033c7\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785111038 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785111038 +0000\n\nfix: validate visual capture project input; host visual docs in dedicat… (#49)\n\n## What\nAdopt the new screencomp release in this repository''s visual-docs\npipeline, so its galleries are hosted in a repository of their own and\nits pull-request comments show real diffs.\n\nFirst determine which screencomp release contains the change. screencomp\nreleases are fully automated: merging to `main` opens a release-plz pull\nrequest that the workflow auto-merges, which tags `vX.Y.Z` and cuts the\nRelease. So the tag may not exist the instant the change merges —\nresolve the newest screencomp release whose commit actually contains the\nexternal-Pages and aggregated-comment work (`gh release list`, `gh\nrelease view`, and the tag''s history), and wait for it rather than\nguessing or pinning a tag that does not exist yet.\n\nThen in `.github/workflows/visual-docs.yml`: advance the\nreusable-workflow ref and `screencomp-version` to that release, and pass\nthe new inputs — `pages-repository:\nnickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site-visual-docs` and the Pages token\nsourced from this repository''s existing `GH_TOKEN` secret (already\nprovisioned with write access to that repository). `comment-mode:\naggregated` and `fail-on-drift: true` stay as they are.\n\nUpdate this repository''s own documentation — `AGENTS.md`, the README,\nand anything under `docs/` that describes the visual-docs loop — to\nstate that galleries now live at\n`https://nickderobertis.github.io/nick-derobertis-site-visual-docs/` and\nwhy: this repository''s own Pages is served from an Actions artifact, so\nits `gh-pages` branch is not served and cannot host them. Leave\n`pages.yml` and the production Pages deploy untouched; that separation\nis the entire reason for the second repository.\n\n## Why\nEvery visual-docs gallery link this repository has ever posted was dead.\nIts Pages site is deployed from an Actions artifact (`build_type:\nworkflow`), so the `gh-pages` branch screencomp deploys galleries to is\nnever served; all twelve links on pull request #47 404''d into the site''s\nown 404 page, which renders the site shell. Pointing screencomp at a\ndedicated Pages repository is what makes visual review work here without\nputting the production site''s deploy at risk.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZqH+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHJsQAANl9t8+VN2FZZVJZ4GW6plH\nc9rAMfuU38qsPEuFOhn+st5btYbOt8ZIaiA7FevKjR776rgrWd1syu+qoa4zSSLb\nCZzyXzIo7d9uSVxtUvtdSvB0YINIUZLN2VE3G154pT9sYSw46xI6y4RybseDAHEA\nWp2xApyc9Vc8tSSHi1sp8GT+sV1Gj50H141eD1/cTyg0u6Y/IbUJlOGr/QhSMYUX\nkq3Gq2zYA4BsrKoEh0uYXu6mc2gxmF8//3eHSkHH