/api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/6bddc6d8e1747714a9397bd6d75265d401bd7a8e"}],"sha":"82b6815c3c6c44129529621e5a8a87de5d4f2159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/82b6815c3c6c44129529621e5a8a87de5d4f2159"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/6bddc6d8e1747714a9397bd6d75265d401bd7a8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T19:37:16Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T19:37:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(loading): render each app''s skeleton during data-loading (#45)\n\n## What\n\nReplace the text data-loading state with each app''s own `<Skeleton>` so\nthe eager Module-Federation fallback and the data-loading render are the\nsame component — one seamless skeleton from remote-fetch through\ndata-fetch, with no text-status flash. Removes the `loading` copy from\neach `State` (error/empty text unchanged) and updates the shell-e2e\nloading assertions to the skeleton. 11 apps + capture harness.\n\n## Why\n\nThe eager skeleton (#38) made remote loading feel instant, but the app\nthen swapped it for a text \"Loading …\" status while data fetched — a\njarring two-step. Reusing the skeleton for the data-loading state gives\none continuous placeholder.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe visual `loading` shots now render the skeleton, so the first CI run\nwill flag loading-baseline drift; the loading baselines are regenerated\nfrom that container capture in a follow-up commit. Recovered from a\ndispatched worker that completed the edits but stalled at closeout.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","tree":{"sha":"18667e49313d368c487975b8c5bef6afcef21744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/18667e49313d368c487975b8c5bef6afcef21744"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/6bddc6d8e1747714a9397bd6d75265d401bd7a8e","verification":{"payload":"tree 18667e49313d368c487975b8c5bef6afcef21744\nparent 683ccdada23fad89524c279841efe5c4171562bc\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1785008236 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785008236 -0600\n\nfeat(loading): render each app''s skeleton during data-loading (#45)\n\n## What\n\nReplace the text data-loading state with each app''s own `<Skeleton>` so\nthe eager Module-Federation fallback and the data-loading render are the\nsame component — one seamless skeleton from remote-fetch through\ndata-fetch, with no text-status flash. Removes the `loading` copy from\neach `State` (error/empty text unchanged) and updates the shell-e2e\nloading assertions to the skeleton. 11 apps + capture harness.\n\n## Why\n\nThe eager skeleton (#38) made remote loading feel instant, but the app\nthen swapped it for a text \"Loading …\" status while data fetched — a\njarring two-step. Reusing the skeleton for the data-loading state gives\none continuous placeholder.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe visual `loading` shots now render the skeleton, so the first CI run\nwill flag loading-baseline drift; the loading baselines are regenerated\nfrom that container capture in a follow-up commit. Recovered from a\ndispatched worker that completed the edits but stalled at closeout.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZRBsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXooQAF3aFPm+4+2PKAbLd7usqFEj\nA1Y28vT2WpHKeBQpw7sn944qzzdCyymevz+woftLZLsk6R0wHGywthJ0rOeCA9sn\nkKb/9Kenu52zwYigG8H5f6YivkwoJQYIUyb6Mikhk8HzP/kn/kpUSS56z5TEji5p\nIiQ2aB2CO0Lq13hO+XoT0/1TPi2tUsOkS2uIDFnxGIy9rdMOsE5687iqcVYCJQj5\nnKFCDB0vHVhiMPQlxwwTZyRPcaugOSPJqiG/eBWVeWvEDC9CEaiV28b36veTIKa0\naBQCx5VUtPDnxIF3wjRJllbOBHxYeFxx6iLqOtypMmYeSrzX+z3yzXNCws8drAD2\n2nQzf/iqAw5ry/o6cTNZWiKKB9/s/2NfBH5AsPVpTs7zFmT3RQnF9aTIecPSdW0G\ntL5D5cL2H+11RayQbWe1hM3FGSSqLp3EJ79076ZEnNTFCVp/TVtvXsuftHsNdUSs\n8xdLxJv4V/bA7Ozn1R6EBtluLKjTpji3EHk6ZaY9btVNnGvvNAhyUl3NZMg9lXL5\n3sdcoepaCS8FXXUKGl3FK7NED0YUtGqbpdS2n+4sQIfneF6DPuz9wo7KnpwyowW6\nszCpBgzmUQ/lQ1jgPsM2669psllenukMXifzTTTKNpPSzmkPyKNI/Vmlwy69cnlv\nr8RhGZpzlGjiXJ2UACad\n=4naO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T19:37:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received