ttps://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/683ccdada23fad89524c279841efe5c4171562bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T16:56:16Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T16:56:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): adopt screencomp aggregated visual comments (v0.4.4) (#44)\n\n## What\n\nBump screencomp to **v0.4.4** and set `comment-mode: aggregated` on the\nreusable visual-docs workflow, so a PR gets **one** combined visual-diff\ncomment covering all affected microfrontends instead of one sticky\ncomment per app (12 → 1). Galleries and GitHub Pages output are\nunchanged.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter adopting the canonical reusable workflow (#42), each PR posted 12\nper-app comments — correct but noisy. screencomp v0.4.4 added an\naggregated single-comment mode; this enables it. Verified locally:\n`verify-visual-contract` passes (all version pins consistent).\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","tree":{"sha":"bece932c150c882ef0adeab4ca7da2f4cc0933b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/bece932c150c882ef0adeab4ca7da2f4cc0933b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/683ccdada23fad89524c279841efe5c4171562bc","verification":{"payload":"tree bece932c150c882ef0adeab4ca7da2f4cc0933b3\nparent a8a946d8768feb02e07c53bf754ab30c90be42e2\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1784998576 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784998576 -0600\n\nfeat(ci): adopt screencomp aggregated visual comments (v0.4.4) (#44)\n\n## What\n\nBump screencomp to **v0.4.4** and set `comment-mode: aggregated` on the\nreusable visual-docs workflow, so a PR gets **one** combined visual-diff\ncomment covering all affected microfrontends instead of one sticky\ncomment per app (12 → 1). Galleries and GitHub Pages output are\nunchanged.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter adopting the canonical reusable workflow (#42), each PR posted 12\nper-app comments — correct but noisy. screencomp v0.4.4 added an\naggregated single-comment mode; this enables it. Verified locally:\n`verify-visual-contract` passes (all version pins consistent).\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZOqwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1QgQAEgvfZm1xrQ7ZHmetwssCt7G\nS1wNPF4EhF3KGtynkJRiYpgjPX+4f+LU11zTYpbxZ7WfP8u/B1ZBIR1Tv1Fc6vUZ\nS1ofh+D9mr0GCfexVBxB6GiFY0FEP/LNJRe1pVzQ3djqLYOQEeJb1a60Iu0Jgay3\nnOHCEZUYDmg7Mt2hfsVTJnJq6EjTEMV66h97kmpXhyPpfNHxSZeR5plwyEoI9f1a\nBT1zT6wiilzTSjUub/jxAI1R7Vm2nHUlFoD4PMe7akhFy91JAIxqa/bvP4AvJ0GL\na7/pdSrhav+51MZVsSyA9oihB4U6evPa0uHtKFZBUzlCB66VpjCRNcfibMq9pK84\ngmFD1jWc16oc3XRxYKqooQPRu5HPwtL7eAY89MaQ2JKxfSD0n7GuDKTUNrB+MtUk\nZEPygaYTO+MViusSHc/b6eWTbiXGI5lsGHnxN5FuxKV0/l7oN/DJS6rA4WaJMgZp\nFIW3Wgjb+guzAicwJYizZwI00x21frDMcOwb2OdQvl/cl1aE3VHE+4DANz3VRe6r\nvqxUQIUqV4ejUxNQaX0WWMcRwBt3AhD7MGzPfNXUkfhfmOqg8PLfCVg1q0KrZOeD\n4x93YBjriFb3sdVfbOVM7z4zUKyIC46e/Lm8+iHrqJLyNbdsRohJLUtfhrjSOMfg\nGwPxVOj6hUnkjDeV4312\n=8OkW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T16:56:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/683ccdada23fad89524c279841efe5c4171562bc","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDY4M2NjZGFkYTIzZmFkODk1MjRjMjc5ODQxZWZlNWM0MTcxNTYyYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/a8a946d8768feb02e07c53bf754ab30c90be42e2","sha":"a8a946d8768feb02e07c53bf754ab30c90be42e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/a8a946d8768feb02e07c53bf754ab30c90be42e2"}],"sha":"683ccdada23fad89524c279841efe5c4171562bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/683ccdada23fad89524c279841efe5c4171562bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/a8a946d8768feb02e07c53bf754ab30c90be42e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T15:29:15Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T15:29:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(ci): adopt canonical screencomp reusable workflow (#42)\n\n## What\n\nAdopt screencomp''s canonical `visual-docs-reusable.yml@v0.4.3` reusable\nworkflow, replacing this repo''s hand-rolled visual-regression pipeline.\nThe new `visual-docs.yml` owns only capture + affected-project selection\n(an upstream `affected` job turns `nx affected --with-target screenshot`\ninto the reusable workflow''s dynamic `projects` matrix — one lane per\naffected microfrontend with its own baseline manifest and gallery);\nscreencomp owns the reproducibility gate, classify drift gate, per-app\ngalleries, Pages deploy, and sticky PR comment. Deletes\n`visual-docs-publish.yml` and the ~7 bespoke scripts\n(`visual-project.sh`, `publish-visual-run.sh`,\n`publish-visual-project.sh`, `inspect-visual-captures.mjs`,\n`resolve-visual-workflow-context.mjs`,\n`write-visual-capture-signal.mjs`) that reimplemented that pipeline.\nAdds `screencomp.toml` + `affected-visual-projects.mjs`; keeps per-app\nbaselines/galleries and the `reference/screenshots` baseline. Net −403\nlines.\n\n## Why\n\nA real-run spike proved screencomp v0.4.2 could not do affected-only\ncapture, so this repo hand-rolled ~2 workflows and ~8 scripts\nduplicating screencomp''s whole pipeline — a large maintenance surface, a\nhost-based capture that flaked cross-environment, and a drift gate (in a\n`workflow_run`) that structurally could not be a required PR check.\nscreencomp v0.4.3 adds affected-only support (`classify --include\nproject=<app>` + a dynamic per-project matrix), so this repo can delete\nthat bespoke code, get deterministic container-based capture, and have a\nsingle canonical classify job that IS a requirable PR check — without\nlosing the affected-only economics.\n\n## Additional info\n\nDepends on `nickderobertis/screencomp@v0.4.3` (Action ref + installed\nCLI pinned to match). After merge, the reusable workflow''s classify job\nbecomes the intended required branch-protection check.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4026f97a9575b518914e2c39b82dc436ac061065","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/4026f97a9575b518914e2c39b82dc436ac061065"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/a8a946d8768feb02e07c53bf754ab30c90be42e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 4026f97a9575b518914e2c39b82dc436ac061065\nparent 39e2dc1bdbcf1fdf33b5406253abc57b47955839\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1784993355 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784993355 -0600\n\nrefactor(ci): adopt canonical screencomp reusable workflow (#42)\n\n## What\n\nAdopt screencomp''s canonical `visual-docs-reusable.yml@v0.4.3` reusable\nworkflow, replacing this repo''s hand-rolled visual-regression pipeline.\nThe new `visual-docs.yml` owns only capture + affected-project selection\n(an upstream `affected` job turns `nx affected --with-target screenshot`\ninto the reusable workflow''s dynamic `projects` matrix — one lane per\naffected microfrontend with its own baseline manifest and gallery);\nscreencomp owns the reproducibility gate, classify drift gate, per-app\ngalleries, Pages deploy, and sticky PR comment. Deletes\n`visual-docs-publish.yml` and the ~7 bespoke scripts\n(`visual-project.sh`, `publish-visual-run.sh`,\n`publish-visual-project.sh`, `inspect-visual-captures.mjs`,\n`resolve-visual-workflow-context.mjs`,\n`write-visual-capture-signal.mjs`) that reimplemented that pipeline.\nAdds `screencomp.toml` + `affected-visual-projects.mjs`; keeps per-app\nbaselines/galleries and the `reference/screenshots` baseline. Net −403\nlines.\n\n## Why\n\nA real-run spike proved screencomp v0.4.2 could not do affected-only\ncapture, so this repo hand-rolled ~2 workflows and ~8 scripts\nduplicating screencomp''s whole pipeline — a large maintenance surface, a\nhost-based capture that flaked cross-environment, and a drift gate (in a\n`workflow_run`) that structurally could not be a required PR check.\nscreencomp v0.4.3 adds affected-only support (`classify --include\nproject=<app>` + a dynamic per-project matrix), so this repo can delete\nthat bespoke code, get deterministic container-based capture, and have a\nsingle canonical classify job that IS a requirable PR check — without\nlosing the affected-only economics.\n\n## Additional info\n\nDepends on `nickderobertis/screencomp@v0.4.3` (Action ref + installed\nCLI pinned to match). After merge, the reusable workflow''s classify job\nbecomes the intended required branch-protection check.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZNZLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ5oQAKIQPePc5NfUrH5dgpbqQBDX\nWLL0QeUwGcKz83u0WK2bklEaXjyruHmhFielQd7eTqSbqP1qzQJ17tDgyPXHyaPK\niuLFZ59pqKrWiB6/S6F2AMDsOAZ5U0d30ctik04Xo7c0KpwZyq8/n1GSM8TIVMJB\nsEkwxbiPOBVdFpcC+PixPkBF+BG5ySm2No/3DtEnIBsMRZxwfbXQcFvISj0awufS\n6TBD4qYpsNRqZVKFxmmY7Rte2mKw+Y1gpedHFVEwmJ6QNWIIH4P5OmTwp88rLl1V\nBNnRpwspHi99ZiqgLfk7EsJj6OzX2S3JO7RuBhMaHlouhsOO5JRExeXlRuhdJXLV\nysV+y7MhtZ4/IgB/a/H8DQWyli/tab7WpugFky77/W243t/DBVPftyFGYFW17kqm\n7MIYMmRi2oINvGAr7n3bZvgHOwd6Dzna49U60QK4KPGd/7foHmYGcRLSAa4tJl/v\nvW3YYe03+NEXkhoRWBqN2DuoeoYNLh9elzGrd2LKHZWzxAqAGDj34PHUXXly7tMF\nnBieDr5aaCwNlGW+CqJ9/gzJaoAqfVosMjfmssy1u9WAK6LPydVO+GxFKcfqYocg\nJXI5BWPKzp0zzH8EQTCqrZmE1ZqQ2Io6kxFoyronmWx9KPp/O061rIPfbP0TApjD\n+fZzHz6es33QA7/pGRpD\n=CpaS\n-----END P