"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/46dee7606c3b88d73276437a5d19e8436fde227d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/7b5a6513879420de8dc3a4b79dd922104629cf70/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T23:15:15Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T23:15:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(skeletons): per-remote loading skeletons, eager fallback (#38)\n\n## What\nGive every microfrontend its own loading skeleton that lives with the\nremote and reflects the remote''s own layout, and have the shell use each\nremote''s skeleton as its Suspense fallback — the skeleton imported\nEAGERLY while the remote itself continues to load LAZILY.\n\n- Each route remote (`home`, `bio`, `research`, `software`, `courses`,\nand any other feature remote the shell composes) exposes a lightweight\n`./Skeleton` module through its Module Federation config, alongside its\nexisting `./Page` expose. The skeleton must be dependency-light (no\n`data-access` domain lib, no heavy chart/deps) so eagerly loading it is\ncheap — it mirrors the remote''s structural layout (header block, card\ngrid, chart placeholder, etc.) as static placeholder shapes.\n- In `apps/shell/src/app.tsx`, replace the single generic\n`RemoteFallback` (\"Loading page…\") with per-route eager skeletons:\nimport each remote''s `Skeleton` eagerly (static `import Skeleton from\n\"<remote>/Skeleton\"`, NOT `lazy`), keep `Page` lazy, and give each route\nits own `<Suspense fallback={<XSkeleton />}>` so the correct app-shaped\nskeleton shows while that remote''s `Page` chunk loads. Remove the\ngeneric `RemoteFallback`.\n- Verify eager-vs-lazy actually holds: the skeleton module must be in\nthe shell''s initial/eager graph and the remote `Page` must remain a\nlazily-fetched chunk. If MF eager sharing needs config (e.g. `eager:\ntrue` on the shared skeleton or a non-lazy remote-module import path),\nwire it and note the mechanism in a comment.\n- Keep standalone-remote render paths working: each remote should still\nrender its own `Page` standalone, and its `Skeleton` should be\nusable/tested standalone too.\n\n## Why\nThe loading UI should live where the structural knowledge lives: each\napp knows its own layout, so it should own the skeleton that mimics it,\nrather than the shell showing one generic \"Loading page…\" for\neverything. Eagerly loading the small skeleton while lazily loading the\napp improves perceived load and gives an accurate structural placeholder\nper feature.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","tree":{"sha":"9ceb8b83fbec3c1c807c04dd70c720608925ff36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/9ceb8b83fbec3c1c807c04dd70c720608925ff36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/7b5a6513879420de8dc3a4b79dd922104629cf70","verification":{"payload":"tree 9ceb8b83fbec3c1c807c04dd70c720608925ff36\nparent d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1784762115 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784762115 -0600\n\nfeat(skeletons): per-remote loading skeletons, eager fallback (#38)\n\n## What\nGive every microfrontend its own loading skeleton that lives with the\nremote and reflects the remote''s own layout, and have the shell use each\nremote''s skeleton as its Suspense fallback — the skeleton imported\nEAGERLY while the remote itself continues to load LAZILY.\n\n- Each route remote (`home`, `bio`, `research`, `software`, `courses`,\nand any other feature remote the shell composes) exposes a lightweight\n`./Skeleton` module through its Module Federation config, alongside its\nexisting `./Page` expose. The skeleton must be dependency-light (no\n`data-access` domain lib, no heavy chart/deps) so eagerly loading it is\ncheap — it mirrors the remote''s structural layout (header block, card\ngrid, chart placeholder, etc.) as static placeholder shapes.\n- In `apps/shell/src/app.tsx`, replace the single generic\n`RemoteFallback` (\"Loading page…\") with per-route eager skeletons:\nimport each remote''s `Skeleton` eagerly (static `import Skeleton from\n\"<remote>/Skeleton\"`, NOT `lazy`), keep `Page` lazy, and give each route\nits own `<Suspense fallback={<XSkeleton />}>` so the correct app-shaped\nskeleton shows while that remote''s `Page` chunk loads. Remove the\ngeneric `RemoteFallback`.\n- Verify eager-vs-lazy actually holds: the skeleton module must be in\nthe shell''s initial/eager graph and the remote `Page` must remain a\nlazily-fetched chunk. If MF eager sharing needs config (e.g. `eager:\ntrue` on the shared skeleton or a non-lazy remote-module import path),\nwire it and note the mechanism in a comment.\n- Keep standalone-remote render paths working: each remote should still\nrender its own `Page` standalone, and its `Skeleton` should be\nusable/tested standalone too.\n\n## Why\nThe loading UI should live where the structural knowledge lives: each\napp knows its own layout, so it should own the skeleton that mimics it,\nrather than the shell showing one generic \"Loading page…\" for\neverything. Eagerly loading the small skeleton while lazily loading the\napp improves perceived load and gives an accurate structural placeholder\nper feature.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYU8DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALQcQAEvGQI7QHO1EJ/tTl1lO9KHO\n0NLmV/gKSLf7vP3BR3+7m14QqL2ymGdanr6CMMFGRGMWZmnXUh4ulLXOvLrrk0Tv\njDZoD0X83uPmSvwvx+/DaESvgP/PSOFPW7VfrX54t7Vg+phtkfqbDv6oQnRHJI8N\nu8hDSO/R4N6CMDDB/GHaPNuzSA7tjUykX4iqT2gpvlJtmhzT/aHm6IzY40mlScEI\nb2JeToWOxy5Nkrt0b4MNWMUMpkKRdrKI7rRGS1X952Wtg95jC/cVH+WsrQPqTjR4\ndfGHSV5QGXzzC+9HlZXx62lLy4NqFyfYiJczx0h0VWBWMCttXRr1oJD1lrvr02GG\noZoHzG7Xf4hemyiTpLAVqhgMo98jyPc066U5wj3ri6NnkjuADLrDvwzfQugdHu2G\nA4CC/TE0yKeH08b/AvV3ZpUSlSOv7Jp374Y7AHT8zyb48eG4Z7KwxasGJOQXdvYu\nSeK9TgSFXLpoU21ZzmX7XY/pi6bj57QNjnSQbLjkOpi+SKO3gpuwMep3AUBaXoRw\nUC4BApb8ug/6LwnChWsho+O3wGOCjMbW3RrVSsKzC5yZeq3dU857WkPyspYIH2xy\ntLet4bKGHwhUbSijXUNfm+I7akw66DglvMyuhXH/0zd+EJAmTK9H1BZ6y9vN0nnB\n5BIGJj1kgrpPz41LUZ5d\n=kSnt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-22T23:15:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/7b5a6513879420de8dc3a4b79dd922104629cf70","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKDdiNWE2NTEzODc5NDIwZGU4ZGMzYTRiNzlkZDkyMjEwNDYyOWNmNzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e","sha":"d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e"}],"sha":"7b5a6513879420de8dc3a4b79dd922104629cf70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/7b5a6513879420de8dc3a4b79dd922104629cf70"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:42:57Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:42:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(nx): centralize local cache outside worktrees (#35)\n\n## What\nMake nx''s local cache live in a stable directory OUTSIDE the\nper-dispatch git worktree, via `NX_CACHE_DIRECTORY`, so cache entries\npersist and are reused across worktrees, retries, and the orchestrator''s\nverification gate instead of being discarded on worktree teardown.\n\n- Set a DEFAULT `NX_CACHE_DIRECTORY` to a stable, host-local,\nrepo-scoped path that resolves to the SAME absolute location for every\nworktree of this repo (e.g. under `$HOME/.cache`), and is overridable by\nan existing env value. The simplest correct place is a top-level `just`\nexport so the registered gate (`just check`) and any direct nx runs all\ninherit it. Do NOT commit a machine-specific absolute path — derive it\n(e.g. from the home directory) or make it env-overridable.\n- It must NOT point inside the worktree (that is the current behavior\nthat breaks reuse) and must be identical across worktrees so they share\none content-hash-keyed cache.\n- Keep `.nx/` gitignored (unchanged).\n- PROVE the win empirically: run the gate once from a cold shared cache\n(populates it), then simulate a second fresh worktree (or delete the\nin-tree `.nx` and re-run) and show the second run gets a high nx\ncache-hit rate from the shared dir — cite the `Cache: X/Y hit (N%)`\nlines before and after. Confirm nx hashes are stable across different\nworktree paths (if they are not, adjust so cross-worktree hits actually\noccur).\n- Document the choice and the concurrency caveat in AGENTS.md (or a\nlinked docs note): a shared nx cache/DB under PARALLEL nx runs can hit\nSQLite lock / FOREIGN KEY contention (observed in this project), so it\nis safe at concurrency 1; for higher concurrency use nx''s proper cache\nlocking or a remote cache.\n\n## Why\nEvery lifecycle dispatch runs in a fresh git worktree, and nx caches to\nthe gitignored `.nx/` INSIDE that worktree, so the cache is thrown away\non teardown and never shared across worktrees, retries, or the\nverification gate. The expensive `nx affected` suite\n(typecheck/test/build/prerender/e2e/screenshot, ~16 min) therefore runs\ncold on essentially every attempt and dominates each node''s wall time.\nCentralizing the cache in a stable shared directory lets a fresh\nworktree on the same commits hit the cache and skip recomputation,\ncutting node latency substantially.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","tree":{"sha":"0af0b2aa43f6736498276c5577f58d4cc9311536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/0af0b2aa43f6736498276c5577f58d4cc9311536"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0af0b2aa43f6736498276c5577f58d4cc9311536\nparent c5314931844a95b66a18c70aae2c5b6ccbc7ba14\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1784691777 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784691777 +0000\n\nperf(nx): centralize local cache outside worktrees (#35)\n\n## What\nMake nx''s local cache live in a stable directory OUTSIDE the\nper-dispatch git worktree, via `NX_CACHE_DIRECTORY`, so cache entries\npersist and are reused across worktrees, retries, and the orchestrator''s\nverification gate instead of being discarded on worktree teardown.\n\n- Set a DEFAULT `NX_CACHE_DIRECTORY` to a stable, host-local,\nrepo-scoped path that resolves to the SAME absolute location for every\nworktree of this repo (e.g. under `$HOME/.cache`), and is overridable by\nan existing env value. The simplest correct place is a top-level `just`\nexport so the registered gate (`just check`) and any direct nx runs all\ninherit it. Do NOT commit a machine-specific absolute path — derive it\n(e.g. from the home directory) or make it env-overridable.\n- It must NOT point inside the worktree (that is the current behavior\nthat breaks reuse) and must be identical across worktrees so they share\none content-hash-keyed cache.\n- Keep `.nx/` gitignored (unchanged).\n- PROVE the win empirically: run the gate once from a cold shared cache\n(populates it), then simulate a second fresh worktree (or delete the\nin-tree `.nx` and re-run) and show the second run gets a high nx\ncache-hit rate from the shared dir — cite the `Cache: X/Y hit (N%)`\nlines before and after. Confirm nx hashes are stable across different\nworktree paths (if they are not, adjust so cross-worktree hits actually\noccur).\n- Document the choice and the concurrency caveat in AGENTS.md (or a\nlinked docs note): a shared nx cache/DB under PARALLEL nx runs can hit\nSQLite lock / FOREIGN KEY contention (observed in this project), so it\nis safe at concurrency 1; for higher concurrency use nx''s proper cache\nlocking or a remote cache.\n\n## Why\nEvery lifecycle dispatch runs in a fresh git worktree, and nx caches to\nthe gitignored `.nx/` INSIDE that worktree, so the cache is thrown away\non teardown and never shared across worktrees, retries, or the\nverification gate. The expensive `nx affected` suite\n(typecheck/test/build/prerender/e2e/screenshot, ~16 min) therefore runs\ncold on essentially every attempt and dominates each node''s wall time.\nCentralizing the cache in a stable shared directory lets a fresh\nworktree on the same commits hit the cache and skip recomputation,\ncutting node latency substantially.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYDxBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWskQABSIN5Ofwc3XQZMWJT0oGAhD\nrXwKt0PUnZwFzY12cxm/yHsKIK1IoZpwwwhF/q+XHJTVqtd/YYaMYpus6HXPA67P\nPfVfCbucuWgAH6Kj/PDgpCKNIzb2hhsnjlcjjZGHe1FDgn/R5Ursv0KLIY6YBSOZ\nyNA4V4kSwPHmZQBdkpRv0anFMwFLw92gy1f//JKiEV65wE7wPal34Waf+2yUUuv/\nLwKwuRYP773mQyxySLtRCP6WfEjSUwqlIqew0cp9YC+fFYn1XP/9BcfyUmPxRyOZ\nKd5//ebY2r7R3ryNTEdF1tzHqvEx1V7pu/BKRxdf4Yr2gI+oxiojOaArs5r0ArKi\nV2ezHcUTS1Qbapu8t9d3KNcB2rZo1YqCLqyU0f4TeHzVD9LjRSdQbw8QdETLYRCt\n8BvYF2FX+FffAvP162Xce5uXyQN5/8oGUK6hiDD35p3ucFgOvxRY9qu/Z/xT+Ra6\nGMpIAK4qM/YEzBGmsQc//fu9bi+44IbLaoaOTwqvjllkcyA/Q5/jGTSDqTAa/MHl\n4uD4iRatGAjT4B6dO+AWHKjFZXjqThM9Irfs+cAy0VeZGBG95Bbq5OrkNizzMb+s\nmhVYMQrTJNM29EhyRWDX9jXJmJGvTN1Y7PdbbW0a5Tcuj3Y4cD0KMSzUrV2m8dJc\n4cmi78tk0Ik1wWzqRnwH\n=db5d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-22T03:42:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commit/d89d5451ee3adb30e28b75b51bcac035a0b4715e","node_id":"C_kwDOEVh7ZNoAKGQ4OWQ1NDUxZWUzYWRiMzBlMjh