0f472","sha":"316b06566bd47b367045a088782425bf5c60f472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/316b06566bd47b367045a088782425bf5c60f472"}],"sha":"0833e14a9053e0a2641b9f06fe829a90501c089e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/0833e14a9053e0a2641b9f06fe829a90501c089e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","id":19440155,"login":"nickderobertis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/commits/316b06566bd47b367045a088782425bf5c60f472/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T14:06:47Z","email":"whoopnip@gmail.com","name":"Nick DeRobertis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T14:06:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: stricter e2e + aggressive-split llmlint rules (#14)\n\n## What\nAuthor the two llmlint rule changes in llmlint.yml for this repo''s\nproof-project bar. This is a FOCUSED config task: do NOT do unrelated\ntooling work. (1) OVERRIDE the inherited e2e/changed-behavior rule (e.g.\nchanged_behavior_has_e2e or e2e_not_mocked) by adding an entry with\n`override: true` and a tightened `description` so the rule holds true\nONLY when every route AND every substantial feature/scenario has a\nreal-browser end-to-end test covering the happy path plus empty,\nloading, and error states, exercised on BOTH the standalone-remote\nrender path and the host-composed render path, driving the real app and\nnever mocking the app under test. (2) ADD a new repo-local rule named\n`microfrontends_split_aggressively` with a clear true/false description:\ntrue when each feature domain is its own Module Federation remote with a\ndeclared Nx project boundary, exposed to the host only at the app/routes\nlayer, with no remote reaching into another remote''s internals and no\nunrelated feature domains bundled into one remote; false otherwise.\nScope its files.include to module-federation configs, rspack configs,\nand project.json, with a `relevance` clause that skips non-remote\nprojects. KEEP the existing scripts/oneharness-fresh.sh plumbing that\nmakes the judge run under bypass mode. Validate the rules parse with\n`just lint-llm-validate` (do NOT run the diff judge here -- the stricter\ne2e rule cannot pass until the microfrontends land). Ensure `just check`\nstill passes. Document both changes briefly in AGENTS.md or a linked\ndoc.\n\n## Why\nDispatched by ai-orchestrator (persona: `engineer`, 1 agent turn(s)),\nverified locally and driven to green checks before merge.\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","tree":{"sha":"78866617d7c2e74502e686a4e26085d4d84cdee0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/trees/78866617d7c2e74502e686a4e26085d4d84cdee0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/nick-derobertis-site/git/commits/316b06566bd47b367045a088782425bf5c60f472","verification":{"payload":"tree 78866617d7c2e74502e686a4e26085d4d84cdee0\nparent 8021cdb9121150a0dd48d5a9dc66a2de5c96fe24\nauthor Nick DeRobertis <whoopnip@gmail.com> 1784556407 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784556407 -0600\n\nchore: stricter e2e + aggressive-split llmlint rules (#14)\n\n## What\nAuthor the two llmlint rule changes in llmlint.yml for this repo''s\nproof-project bar. This is a FOCUSED config task: do NOT do unrelated\ntooling work. (1) OVERRIDE the inherited e2e/changed-behavior rule (e.g.\nchanged_behavior_has_e2e or e2e_not_mocked) by adding an entry with\n`override: true` and a tightened `description` so the rule holds true\nONLY when every route AND every substantial feature/scenario has a\nreal-browser end-to-end test covering the happy path plus empty,\nloading, and error states, exercised on BOTH the standalone-remote\nrender path and the host-composed render path, driving the real app and\nnever mocking the app under test. (2) ADD a new repo-local rule named\n`microfrontends_split_aggressively` with a clear true/false description:\ntrue when each feature domain is its own Module Federation remote with a\ndeclared Nx project boundary, exposed to the host only at the app/routes\nlayer, with no remote reaching into another remote''s internals and no\nunrelated feature domains bundled into one remote; false otherwise.\nScope its files.include to module-federation configs, rspack configs,\nand project.json, with a `relevance` clause that skips non-remote\nprojects. KEEP the existing scripts/oneharness-fresh.sh plumbing that\nmakes the judge run under bypass mode. Validate the rules parse with\n`just lint-llm-validate` (do NOT run the diff judge here -- the stricter\ne2e rule cannot pass until the microfrontends land). Ensure `just check`\nstill passes. Document both changes briefly in AGENTS.md or a linked\ndoc.\n\n## Why\nDispatched by ai-orchestrator (persona: `engineer`, 1 agent turn(s)),\nverified locally and driven to green checks before merge.\n\nCo-authored-by: nick <nick@U-17UN402ICR95C.workspaces.hellopatient.internal>","rea